The President of Russia Vladimir Putin signed a law on the introduction of administrative responsibility for violation of the term and procedure for payment of goods (works, services) when carrying out purchases for state and municipal needs.
This law is designed to solve a very acute problem of non-performance of their obligations by customers in the implementation of state and municipal procurement.
Yet two years ago the situation when entrepreneurs could not receive payment on already fulfilled state and municipal contracts was ubiquitous.
At the same time the President of Russia instructed the General Prosecutor’s Office of the Russian Federation to take the problem for special control.
Because the businessmen themselves could not cope with unscrupulous customers, who concluded contracts not backed by financing, in every possible way tried to evade the obligations to pay and included illegal conditions in the contracts.
The problem was systemic in the country as a whole.
Since 2015, in the interests of protecting the rights of erprise to receive payment under public orders by the prosecutor's office made 9.7 thousand submissions, according to the results of their consideration, 4.5 thousand officials were brought to disciplinary responsibility, 533 were brought to the administrative authorities, 75 materials have been submitted to the investigative bodies for the organization of procedural checks, 46 of them have initiated criminal cases.
As a result, the arrears to entrepreneurs in the amount of more than 66 billion rubles were repaid.
And these huge sums accumulated not as a result of non-payment of multi-billion-dollar contracts.
fabulous oblivities led to numerous, systematic delays in the payment of services to entrepreneurs with much more modest amounts.
That's a characteristic case.
The head of a small company won the competition for the provision of social transportation services for several million rubles.
A person has invested all his negotiable funds, has fully complied with its obligations, but he did not receive the required money on time.
The result - the growing financial group of the arrears on wages, taxes, loans that would lead to bankrupt, if the entrepreneur did not apply for help to the prosecutor's office.
Now in a number of regions the problem was minimized.
Nevertheless, as of the first half of 2017, the cumulative amount of debt on state and municipal contracts, identified by prosecutors of the constituent entities of the Russian Federation, amounted to about 27.4 billion rubles.
In the regions where the indicators of debts continue to reach critical values, the prosecutor's office is operating in the manual anti-crisis management.
The procurator-general personally conducts visiting meetings with representatives of the local authorities, at which all irregularities opened by the procurators and measures to immediately eliminate them are met.
Such operational meetings this year have already taken place in Yaroslavl and Yekaterinburg.
Qualitatively improve the payment discipline of public russians will the implementation of Federal law No. 189-FZ “On Amendments to the Code of the Russian Federation on Administrative Offenses regarding the establishment of administrative responsibility of the customer’s officials for a violation and the procedure for paying for goods (works, services) when carrying out purchases to provide state and municipal needs”, which was signed last week by the President of Russia.
The draft of the law was developed by the Ministry of economic development of Russia on the initiative of the Prosecutor-Guard.
The new law will be supplemented by the Code of the Russian Federation on administrative offenses with an article, which stipulates a fine from 30 thousand to 50 thousand rubles for a violation by an official of the customer of the period and the procedure for paying for goods, works and services during state and municipal procurement.
And if the official has already been subjected to an administrative punishment for a similar offense, he will be disqualified for a period of from one to two years.
All procurators of the constituent entities of the Russian Federation have already received an order to ensure the implementation of these legislative novels in practice.
The Civil Rights Protection Group Annlarifies War on Moving to Missouri
The National Choosing Development Association has issued a warning for colored people traveling to Missouri because of discriminatory state-of-policies and racist attacks.
“Waiting warnings to traveling the National Cholergy Association, valid until August 28, 2017, calls on Afro-American travellers, guests and Missouri citizens to be especially attentive to be especially attentive when traveling around the state in connection with a number of dubious racist incidents that have recently taken place throughout the state.”
According to the National Companion of Facilitating the Progress of the People of color, the group has prompted the recently passed in Missouri law, which made it more difficult for people to win claims related to discriminance, as well as the fact that law enforcement agencies disproportionately choose representatives of members of minorities.
“People are subject to human rights violations.
They are stopped on the roads because of the color of their sneezing, they are beaten and murdered,” Rod Chepel, president of the National Association for Propagãation for the Progress of Industrious Mosquot, told Kansas-City of the Old Town.
“We’ve often heard complaints more than ever before.”
This is the first warning of this kind, announced by the organization in relation to the state of the United States.
The group referred to such incidents as humiliating black students on a racial basis at the University of Missouri and the death of twenty-eight-year-old Tory Sanders, a black man from Tennessee.
Sanders died under suspicious circumstances earlier this year, after he ran out of petrol during a state trip, and Missouri police arrested him without being charged with a crime.
The warning also mentions a recent report by the Office of Missouri Attorney-Reserve, according to which it is 75 per cent more likely to be stopped on the road for red-and-floating drivers than for whites.
“The purpose of the warning is that the people are aware of the situation and to warn their relatives and friends and co-workers about what could happen in Missouri,” Chapel said.
“Men must be prepared in one way or another whether they will take money for the pledge, or tell their relatives that they are traveling through the territory of the state.”
According to the latest information of the FBI’s Hate-Trafficking Crimes program, 100 hate crimes were registered in Missouri in 2015, making the staff sixteen in the state the number of such violations.
A traffic warning is also a response to a new Missouri law, after which it will become more difficult to initiate a case against a legal entity in connection with housing or labor discrimination.
The American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) has previously issued warnings to traveling in Texas and Arizona after these states enacted new immigration control laws, according to which local law enforcement agencies were ordered to arrest people for violation of immigration laws, which, according to ACLU, was supposed to increase the number of checks on racial grounds.
Travel warnings are usually issued by the State Department in relation to other countries, but recently, public organizations have resorted to this measure in response to certain laws and trends within the U.S.
