Vladimir Putin instructed to dismantle Baikal pollution
The President of Russia Vladimir Vladimir Putin at a meeting on the protection of Baikal said that in recent years significant areas of the lake have been subjected to extreme pollution.
He instructed to identify sources of financing, plans and executors to eliminate pollution.
Mr. Putin also instructed to carry out a full-fledged reclamation of the polluted territories.
“It is also Necessary to deal with the objects that continue to work, the simulus structures of the majority of them are exhausted”, – quotes “RIA Novosti” the President.
He also added that the General Prosecutor’s office of Russia should carry out an inspection to identify environmentally harmful activities.
According to him, there are problems associated with the emergence of natural landfills and a number of violations in the field of ecology on the part of recreation organizers.
“I want to emphasize this: not to check everything in a row, you also need to know a measure here, but it’s an illegal and environmentally harmful activities and take appropriate measures,” he said.
Earlier, the Prosecutor General’s office announced the reduction of fish inventories in Lake Baikal and proposed to increase the number of objects falling under environmental supervision.
We will remind, on June 15 Vladimir Putin during a straight line announced the need to change the legislation to ensure the rights of citizens living in the natural territories of a special security regime.
About the problems with the conduct of economic activities he was informed by the inhabitants of the island of Olkhon, which is part of the Baikal natural territory.
The President of the Ministry of Natural Resources Sergey Donskoy immediately proposed to solve the problem by clarifying the boundaries of the water protection zone of Baikal, but the government of Buryatia recalled that such a change is not enough, since the restrictions are associated with a number of normative acts.
Earlier in the Ministry of economy proposed to solve the problem by changing the land code and the law on the protection of the environment.
