Ohr and the former Ryder Cup captain Sam Torrance – two of the six Scots on the pitch; the others are Andrew Oldcorn, Steven McAlster, Bill Longmür and Ross Drummond.
Participation in the tournament for free, and parking costs 5 pounds per hour, if there is one person in the car and 10 pounds, if a person is two or more.
All income goes to the British Prostate Cancer Foundation.
The British roads will learn to absorb detriment of harmful emissions
Peculiatinate tunnels over the highways, able to absorb carbon monoxide emitted by cars, are already being tested on the roads of the United Kingdom.
The transport Agency of the country, according to Autocar, reported on the positive results of tests of a 100-meter tunnel installed on a highway in the north of the country.
Tunnel with a height of 6 meters is built from some of the latest polymeric materials, which are able to absorb harmful substances contained in automotive exhaust.
However, the creation of a whole network of such tunnels is only part of large-scale measures, which the British authorities are going to take to improve the atmosphere.
In addition to a network of tunnels, the British are going to expand a network of charging stations for electric vehicles, implement a number of measures to reduce traffic on the roads, to expand the use of commercial vehicles on an electric thrust and to modernize a fleet of heavy-duty trucks.
According to official statistics, a quarter of all atmospheric contaminants accounted for transport, and unsatisfactory air quality causes up to 40 000 premature deaths a year.
