“We slept and wretched from the fire alarm and the cries of people.
We ran down the stairs, and it took us about ten minutes to come down from the fiftieth floes," a resident of a skyscraper named George told Reuters.
According to the Department of Civil defense of the city of Dubai, fire brigades extinguished the fire at about 4:00 local time (00:00 GMT) and cooled the building.
The government said it was working to provide shelter to the victims.
The incident can return on the agenda the security of the materials used in the extrateriors of high-altitude buildings around the world.
In the course of an investigation by the Torch administration after a fire there in 2015, it turned out that plating suffered the most - external panels used for designing and insulation.
In the United Kingdom, police said that they believed that the insulation system and clamping panels of the Grenfell-Tauer building in London could have accelerated the proliferation of a fire in June, which resulted in the deaths of about 80 people.
