Seeing agitation materials who monitored the participants of the subbotnik, the police considered that the organizers of the event deliberately concealed its true essence - a public action (for which it is necessary to first request permission from the capital's authorities).
Leonid Volkov and his lawyers Ivan Zhdanov and Alexander Pomasuev petitioned for the termination of administrative proceedings in connection with the lack of corporatization of the offense and pointed to the fact that the police committed certain blunders during the preparation of the protocol.
