The Agency for Environmental Protection after lawsuits abrogates the decision to postpone the adoption of a law on air pollution
The American Environmental Protection Agency has canceled the decision to postpone the adoption of an anti-Official law, according to which states should limit air polluting emissions a day after 15 states seduced to the agency because of this step.
