Two-Yad-old after the Peak of the migratory Crisis in Europe, Italy decided on a limited military operation in the Mediterranean.
Patrol ship "Commandate Borsini" entered the territorial waters of Libya in order to stop the influx of illegal migrants.
The decision to begin the operation was made by the Italian parliament on Wednesday.
Rome agreed it with the internationally recognized Libyan government, which, however, does not control much of the country.
A stand-alone cabinet and the Tubruk-based Libyan parliament accused Italy of violating Libya’s sovereignty.
And the commander of the Libyan National Army, Field Marshal Haftar gave his subordinate an order to oppose the Italian ships.
In Rome, however, said that they do not believe these threats and intend to slept another military vessel into Libyan territorial waters.
The situation was discussed last last week at the negotiations of the Italian Prime Minister Paolo Gentilono and the head recognized by the Libyan cabinet Faiz Sarraj.
The authorities of Italy went to establish a naval mission to combat illegal migration after statistics was published in July on the number of illegal immigrants who have sailed into the country from Libya: 95 thousand people since the beginning of the year.
In the government stated that resources for accepting migrants have been exhausted.
