How the financial rules of football will influence Neymar’s move to Paris
Rules aimed at preventing unlimited waste from European football clubs will not interfere with a world-registered transfer of Neymar from the Spanish “Barcelona” in the French “Paris Saint-Germain”.
Whatever the consequences can come further along the chain, for “Pari Saint-Germain” by UEFA, the governing body controlling European football, in whose power to forbade the teams to participate in the Prestigious “Champions League tournament”.
From the rules of financial “fair play”, introduced by UEF in 2011, it follows that PSG will finally have to show that Neymar’s transfer was financed without major losses.
“Barcelone” paid 222 million euros ($ 222 million) just to ousting the Brazilian from the contract, and Neymar will receive a salary that will reach tens of millions of dollars a year.
Here are some financial aspects of Neymar's move to France.
PSG can definitely fork to hire Neymar and add it to the galaxy of other stars, taking into account the team's funding from the energy-footed Qatari family.
“Cubs have the right to spend large sums to acquire players, but they have to balancing them through legitimate sources of income in order to reach the threshold of profitability in their football business.
“FFP” introduced Michel Platini after he was elected president of UEFA in 2007.
The former French footballer believed that clubs climbing into huge debt in their thirst for success, in essence, cheated and risked a devastation in the event that the banks or owners ceased the financing.
In 2011, “FFP” ceased to focus on the debts of the clubs and instead switched to tracing their losses.
As a result of this change, the business model originally used by Roman Abramovich in Chelsea in 2003 - to buy a club with good potential, and then to spend seriously in order to improve the team and to create a global brand - has become a difficult-performing plan.
During this three-annorth appraisal punctuation period 2018, clubs can insufficient losses of €30 million.
And, although Platini was disgracedly removed from the presidency in 2015, his successor at UEFA Alexander Ceferin is still determined to restrain excessive spending.
“Therefore, “FFP is alive, and we, moving forward, will tighten the rules,” Andrea Traverso said last last week, which controls FFP in U.P.
Although “PSG” will repurchase Neymar at a minimum time, he can distribute this amount for reporting on the entire length of his contract.
Neymar signed a five-Yieging contract, so that the transfer value can be shown in annual reports as a cost of 44.4 million euros over the next five years.
During the First Wave of FFP Sanctations in 2014, PSG, as well as Abu Dhabi, heavy sanctions were sanctioned.
PSG imposed a fine of 60 million euros (at that rate of $82 million), which was later reduced to 20 million euros, and it was ordered to limit the line-of-commandment of his team at the Champions League during the 2014-1015 season with 21 players instead of the usual 25.
Uafa is tracking clubs that can try to outsmart its financial inspection by inflating their income from companies affiliated with club owners.
Although the Catarrhal company could responsive PSG, but if the amount of funding was considered higher than the standard market prices, UEFA would not allow it to be considered a legitimate income.
This is exactly what Happened in 2014, when U.A. UEFA decreed that the amount of PSG funding from the Qatar Tourism Authority was indulgence.
It was reported that part of Neymar's earnings in PSG could come in the form of payments from the organizing committee of the world Cup 2022 in Qatar.
But PSG and Qatar 2022 deny that Neymar will become an ambassador of the World Cup, and such a manoeuvre could easily be detected by UEFA inspectors.
Past Sanctions Imposed on PSG mean that UEFA will be even more attentive to monitor any attempts to circumvent the rules.
As reported on Thursday by persons familiar with the situation, UEFA did not conduct a preliminary discussion with “PSG” about the transfer of Neymar.
They communicated with the Assoshiated P.P. agency on condition of announity, as it is not authorized to discuss PSG regulation.
According to the latest published reports, in 2015-1016 PSG received more than 10 million euros of profit with a turnover of 542.4 million euros.
Receivables have not yet been published for the last fiscal year.
PSG awaits Neymar ' s arrival will become a fertile basis for sponsorship deals, selling paraphernalia and t-shirts with a team logo.
In the club assume that the turnover will grow by at least 30 percent due to the hiring of a new player.
Undeniably angry that one of the best players leaves, the Spanish league tried to thwart Neymar transfer, stating that PSG will violate the financial “Fair play”.
“It’s an obvious ‘financial doping’, with the club and the state,” La Liga President Javier Tebas said in view that Qatar is the ultimate owner of PSG.
The coach of “Arsenal” Arsene Wenger, whose club belongs to an American sports tycoon, shares the doubts of La Liga regarding the financing of the club by the state.
“It’s all the consequences of equity participation, and it has completely changed the landscape of football in the last fifteen years,” Wenger said.
“When the club belongs to the country, everything is possible.
It becomes very difficult to observe the financial fair play, because the country can have a lot of ways and there are a lot of reasons to be represented by such a serious player.
Arrcipal and places of taking the oath will be determined by the President
where and how new Russian citizens will swear allegiance of the Russian Federation will be determined - such amendments for the second reading in the relevant law was developed by the State Duma Committee on Legislation and State Construction.
A week ago, the deputies planned to directly determine the procedure for taking an oath in the law.
Children under the age of 18, as well as incapacitated, follows from the finalized text of the amendments to the bill “On citizenship of the Russian Federation” (“Izvestia”) (available to “Izvestia”), which the committee on July 11 will consider before the second reading at its meeting.
The idea of introducing an octophemy when joining the citizenship of the Russian Federation instead of the formal signing of the documents, President Vladimir Vladimir Putin supported on June 6 during a meeting with the speaker of the state Duma Vyacheslav Volodin.
Deputies issued this idea in the form of an amendment for the second reading to the bill, which provides for the abolition of the decision on the granting of citizenship to those who were subsequently convicted of a number of crimes of a terrorist or extremist nature: for example, for public incitement to terrizzard to terrism or its public justification in the media or on the Internet (part 2 of article 205.2 of the criminal code of the Russian Federation), as well as for the hijacking of an aircraft, a train or a water transport, but - only in the case.
According to the bill, its logic was as follows: when registering documents for citizenship, a person is signed on a promise to comply with Russian legislation - embarking on the path of extremism, he violates this promise.
The bill in April was submitted to the state Duma by the leaders of the Duma Vladimir Vasilyev (“United Russia”), Gennady Zyuganov (CPRF), Vladimir Zhirinovsky (LDPR), Sergei Mironov (“Fair Russia”) and the speaker of the State Duma Vyacheslav Volodin.
On May 19, the deputies accepted him in the first reading.
Last week last week, the State Duma Committee on State-Salvation and Legislature approved the text of the bill for the second reading, but now it has been recycled once again.
Now it is said that the procedure for taking an oath will be established by the President of the Russian Federation.
Earlier, parliamentarians were going to describe the procedure directly in the law “On the citizenship of the Russian Federation”, pointing out that the ceremonies should take place in a ceremonial situation in a solemn atmosphere in front of the state coat of arms and the flag of Russia in the presence of a representative of the Ministry of internal Affairs.
However, it was not clear from the text of the bill where such an event should take place - the list of places where it is Possible to place the coat of arms of the Russian Federation is regulated by the relevant federal constitutional law.
Among them are the courts, the offices of the heads of state authorities of subjects, municipalities, judges, prosecutors, the heads of federal executive bodies, etc.
Most likely, it could also be registrars.
To pronounce ceremonial o'circumbag wishing to obtain Russian citizenship after the officials will verify their documents.
But a person will receive a Russian passport only after taking an o'clock, it follows from the revised text.
A week ago in the project it was said that the oath should precede the signing of a decree.
In the updated text it is said about the fact that Russia will be sworn in from the age of 18, and not with 14.
There is a rule according to which occupies-of-capital or limited permissible, as well as those who cannot pronounce, read or personally sign the text of the oath will be freed from taking an o'clock.
In addition, the President of the Russian Federation has the right to exempt from this procedure and “other persons”,
The updated bill stipulates a special procedure for the admission of residents of Ukraine to Russian citizens, who are considered carriers of the Russian language.
They will have to officially renounce Ukrainian citizenship, providing a corresponding statement to the authorized body of Ukraine for this.
Notarially certified acovid recognizion of the application will need to be handed over to Russian officials.
Refusal of “foreign” citizenship, as it does now, will not be required, if this is provided for by an international treaty or if this is not possible “for reasons independent of the person”.
The corresponding amendments to the law were proposed by a group of deputies, including First Vice-Specist of the state Duma Ivan Melnikov (CPRF), Natalia Poklonskaya, Pavel Krasheninnikov and Ayrat Farrakhov (all - "United Russia").
I think that many of you know that to get a certificate from Ukraine is unrealistic, it is simply impossible.
Accordingly, a lot of people are waiting to decide their fate regarding the citizenship of the Russian Federation, – explained on the day the day the head of the Duma Committee on state construction and legislation Pavel Krasheninnnikov (EP).
In addition, in the text there was a refinement that the restrictions on occupying certain positions for foreigners will do not apply to those who renuled “another” citizenship in writing and handed over a previous passport to the Ministry of internal Affairs of the Ministry of internal Affairs of the Russian Federation, but “for reasons beyond the control of him”, he did not cease to be considered a citizen of another country.
Now foreigners are prohibited from occupying positions in the municipal service, to be hired to work for objects and organizations whose activities are associated with ensuring the security of Russia.
Also, a person with dual citizenship or a residence permit of another country can not become a deputy of the state Duma or a member of the Federation Council.
It is planned that the law should enter into force from September 1, 2017, by that time the necessary sub-laws must be prepared.
Nostalgia becomes niche in “Hot American Anniversary Anniversary”
The current iteration of history is nostalgically reminisceptable at the same time about the glorious days of the characters in the 80s; the era of the grunge in the 90s (approximation at a time when the outstanding masters David Wayne and Michael Schovalter made a comedy of sketches for MTV); and about myself - that is, about 2001, before its stars, like Elizabeth Banks, Amy.
As the fact of culture, it is at the same time the elevation and incarnation of our epoch with its constant reministinations from Facebook.
But as a franchise it seems an anachronism.
"The first day of the camp" was surprisingly good, and not only because of the an absurdist humor (including the original story about the talking jar of vegetables, which was voiced by J. John Benjamin).
The result doubles the main joke: middle-aged actors play sexually annoyed children who have just reached the age of majority; due to this, the inability to return becomes part of a joke.
“Ten Years Later”, where adults have already played adults, has areverage less deep emotional roots, and its parody is more haphazard and includes riffs from stalke films of the 90-ies such as “Harbow Moving the Cradle”.
One-episode character wears an Apple Powerbook, four-wheeled skating skates and “a bunch of other things from 1991”.
