Victor (Ken Marino) still hasn’t parted virginity.
And here there is still an insane and despicable conspiracy in which Ronald Reagan participates (also Shawaulter), which is now incited by George H.U. Sr. (a parody performed by Michael Blank).
As always, the best part of the franchise is to turn away from it.
Particularly funny is to see an eternally young Rudd, who sing Matt Dillon’s songs from “Lones”, the character of which the former big man Andy now looks like an old man.
To bring to this franchise the success, random insanity in the spirit of the type the recursive series "Seven Up", while it does not reach the fact that, in my opinion, it would be its logical conclusion: "Hot American summer: twenty years later", where in the last scene the whole company would go to the cinema at the premiere of the film "Hot American summer".
"Comrade Detective" on the Amazon refers to another type of nostalgia: memories of the cold war from “Americans”, “Explosive blondes” or even “brilliance” with her images of the struggle of the East and the West.
This comedia created by Brian Gatewood and Alessandro Tanaka with director Rize Thomas depicts a telefilm: a Romanian policeace drama of the 80's about two police officers in Bucharest who are fighting for the truth, atheism and the Marxist-Leninist path.
The main roles - Gregor who has seen the life and idealist Josef - are performed by Florin Piercique Jr. and Cornelius Ulitch, and voiced their dialogues in English Channing Tatoum (aka executive producer) and Joseph Gorgdon-Lewit.
It's shiny idea.
It's just an idea.
There are a number of visual jokes (politicians spend time watching the chess match, as the Americans could watch football).
The team of the famous voiced - among them Jenny Slate, Nick Offerman, Maherschal Ali and Chloe Sevignia - allows you to interestingly play "guess up your voice".
"Comrade Detective" so clings to the plausibility of a clumsy propaganda drama - there is even a killer in Ronald Reagan's masquote - which often looks like her.
Six long episodes are delayed, and it does not happen so much and not often.
If he was shorter, "Comrade Detective" could better cope with his satire in the spirit of agitprop; for example, every time Gregor and Josef come to an American embassy, there are two fat people who absorb a lot of hamburgers.
The imaginary specturer-communist says this image that Western culture is able to make an enromentation from anything.
Fictitious Romanian authors of the film are not so unrighteous: We are doing so even with our own recent history, and with them too.
