The Bank of England will maintain interest rates at 0.25%
It is expected that the Bank of England will later announcing that interest rates will not change after faint economic growth and weakening inflation has caused rubbreas to circulate about a possible increase.
The Bank of England warned that economic growth will remain unsustainable, leaving interest rates unchanged from growing pressure on family gains.
Specialists of the Bank's Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) voted with a score of 6 against 2 for maintaining rates of 0.25%, and this month a smaller number of committee members were in favor of increasing the rate, because weak economic growth has weakened support for the increase.
In its quarter-way report on inflation, the bank limited its forecasts by an increase of 1.7% percent in 2017 and 1.6% in 2018 and warned that the pressure on family incomes will continue, while inflation is still expected to rise to about 3% in the fall.
However, the bank warned that rate hikes in the next few years will be necessary to control inflation caused by brquet-induced inflation, and said it is likely that borrowing costs will have to rise more than expected in financial markets.
Also, the members of the committee voted to renounce part of a huge complex of measures for the development of the economy, launched a year ago because of Brexit.
Beginning the next February, the bank will close an urgent financing plan, according to which it provides banks with Cheap Loaves, although it has announced that it will now provide another 15 billion pounds to 115 billion pounds as part of this plan.
“According to MPC’s main predictions, the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) growth continues to be slow in the near future, while the pressure on real family income continues to affect consumption.”
On besuing besuing bets, he repecreated that in order to oust inflation, it would take “some tougher financial policies” in a “several increase” than the markets expected.
At the moment, the markets predict the first increase in the third quarter of next-and-furish year and another in 2020.
But the bank stressed that all the increases will be “decreased” and “restricted”.
Forecasts of the bank for an increase in this and next year is lower than the forecasts made in May, which were equal to 1.9% and 1.7%.
The bank left unchanged its forecast by 1.8% in 2018.
After this news, sterling fell in relation to the dollar and the euro.
The pound fell 0.5% to 1.31 U.S. dollars and 0.4% to 1.11 euros.
The decision not to change the bet was made after the recent dissolutive indicators of growth weakened the increased expectation of an increase; then GDP grew by 0.3% in the second quarter against 0.2% in the previous three months.
According to the representative of the representative of the bank, the growth, apparently, will remain at 0.3% in the third quarter, although it will begin to increase a little at the end of the year.
The bank's latest report on inflation gave little reason for the joy of households, which was affected by high inflation and very small wage increases: according to the bank, the pressure will increase before falling.
The bank added that the financial policy “can’t be awaiting” the denunciation of earnings in the next few years, but it expects that wages “significantly” will recover by the end of its three-year forecast.
The economy is also tuned to growth as a result of the growing demand for British goods, due to the low pound, which compensates for part of reduced consumer spending.
The decision was made a year after last August the rates were reduced to 0.25% after the shocking results of the referendum on leaving the European Union, resulting in a pound drop.
According to the bank, it is most likely to take a four-year-old to fully affect prices and the economy.
Before the bank rendered its last decision on the bets, there was a buoyant around the alleged rate hike, as inflation put more and more pressured domestic households: three members of the committee of specialists asked to raise the rates to 0.5% in July.
Inflation last month fell to 2.6% from 2.9% in July, although, according to the bank, this fall was expected to be offset in the coming months again.
According to the bank, a higher indicator compared to the planned 2% is completely a consequence of a low pound.
Andrew Montlaek, director of Mortgage Brokers Koreko, said: “If you take into account the recent fall in swap, the mortgage market appears to become even more competitive again, as lenders demand business opportunities and look forward for a good end of the year.
The market looks especially favorable for those who are approaching the graduation of their existing contracts, since refinancing of loans, often with the possibility of no commission, as well as at a low bet, is becoming more popular than ever.”
The public health service will prescribe a dissolution drug against HIV 10000
Beginning in September, patients will have access to a “revolutionary” drug for the prevention of HIV after the battle in the High Court on the issue of financing the drug from the public health service.
The National Health Service of England announced that pre-exposure HIV prophylaxis (PES), a pill taken before sex that has been proven to reduce the risk of infection in persons at risk by an average of 86 per cent, will now be provided by a health service within an initial three-year probabilization of about 10,000.
She agreed to finance the test after an appellate court upheld last-announced Supreme Court ruling, which claimed that the National Health Service had the opportunity to pay for the AES, despite her claims that it should be financed by local authorities.
This step, announced on Thursday, was called “the most powerful innovation” of the President of the National Health Service of England Simon Stevens, and the National AIDS Dispensal Control Authority (NAT) called it a “turning point”.
“Before releasing the program throughout England by April 2018, venerological dispensaries in London, Briston, Manchester, Liverpool and Sheffield are among the first to start releasing people and more dispensaries will join the program in October.
Pre-exposure prophylaximation is a course of HIV drugs taken before sex to reduce the risk of contracting HIV.
As studies have been shown to have shown, PRES significantly reduces the risk of HIV infection among people at risk.
When taking PPP before sex in the human body a sufficient amount of certain drugs to prevent infection with HIV infection.
Such drugs can be taken every day or no later than two hours before sex.
Patients who are entitled to the drug include homosexual and bisexual men, transgender persons and people whose partners are HIV-positive and don't receive successful treatment.
Dispensary will select suitable participants who agreed to participate, including men, women, transgender people, and persons about whose partners it is not known whether their HIV status with antiretroviral therapy is restrained.
People who live and are attributed to the general practitioner in England will also be able to apply for potential participation in the nearest venéric dispensary taking part in the program.
The program will cost 10 million pounds, and the National Health Service of England this week after an international procurement tender has signed a drug-providing agreement.
The study is structured in such a way as to assess all the possibilities of PrEP by collecting clinical data on who the target audience of the drug, its digestibility and application on a large scale.
“This crucial innovation should complement and strengthen large-scale and increasingly successful efforts aimed at preventing HIV.
This is another milestone in more than three decades of stedrance in the fight against one of the greatest threats to the health that humanity faces.
Deborah Gahld, President of NAT, said: “It’s a turning point in the fight against HIV.
PrEP, appropriately targeting people who are in need of assistance and at-to-risk, makes it necessary to change the situation with the HIV epidemic in England.
Beginning in Septe, people at risk for HIV, thanks to this study, conducted in England at the expense of the National health service, will have access to a newly opened up new-enable tool, the use of which a person can control himself without discussing this with a partner, which will lead to the improvement of many, many lives.
We warmly welcome this news.”
Yan Green, president of Terrence Higgins Foundation, said: “Now we need to take care that the test quickly unfurled all over the country, so that none at risk for HIV should be forgotten.
Now, when we’re backed by an experimental PREP drug we’re going to protect more than 10,000 people at risk for HIV.”
Sharon Hodgson, the Shadow Minister for People's Attitude, said: "We very much welcome the beginning of the PrEP test, it is too late due to months of delays and pro-concessions from the government."
Evidence demonstrates how reluctating this drug can become as part of our approach to preventing HIV and stopping the transmission of this fatal infection.
This test will bring us a step closer to a complete understanding of the benefits of PEP.
Now it's important that the trial is deployed as soon as possible throughout the country, in order to protect persons at risk of HIV and advance us a step towards stopping the spread of HIV in society.
The World Tatar Congress adopted a resolution to support the Treaty of Tatarstan and Russia
The Sixth Congress of the World Tatar Congress adopted a resolution, in which he noted the importance of retaining the presidency in Tatarstan.
According to the document, the post is “positively established for the organization of the highest state power in the Republic and expresses the national interests of the entire Tatar people”.
In addition, the Congress emphasized in the resolution the importance of an agreement on the demarcation of powers between Russia and Tatarstan.
According to the document, he "played a positive role in the ethno-cultural, socio-economic and socio-political development of Tatarstan and the Russian Federation as a Whole."
The agreement between Moscow and Kazan in force since July 24, 2007, has been concluded for 10 years.
On July 11, the deputies of the State Council of Tatarstan appealed to the President of Russia with a request to extend the agreement and retain the name of the position of the head of the region.
Tatarstan is now the only subject of the federation that has an agreement with Russia.
The head of the region - the only, whose position is called "president".
In Russia there were difficulties in obtaining an international driving license
Traffic units are experiencing a shortage of international driver's licenses (IDPs).
To obtain such rights, you have to wait for the queue for several weeks, which has become a real problem for vacationers who want to go on a vacation abroad on their own car or take it there for rent.
It is worth noting that the situation with international driving licenses remains contradictory.
The IDP was enacted in order to make it easier for the foreign police to make it easier to understand what is written in the national certificate, since the information is explained in five languages.
Requirements for international rights are recorded in the 1968 Vienna Convention on Road Traffic, but in countries that corroborated by the Vienna Convention, Russian rights are recognized so.
However, in fact, everything depends on a specific police or rental office: some require an IDP, and someone has enough national rights.
To insecure, drivers still receive international rights, but it should be borne into account that countries that do not corroat the convention (for example, the United States, Spain, Mexico, Indonesia), the authorities do not have the right to recognize either national rights or IDPs.
Now there is a problem with the forms in almost all units of the traffic police, Kommersant reports, after conducting a study in a number of regions.
So, in Moscow, coupons are simply not issued, forms have not expired for four months already.
You can register for an reception on the website of public services, but the queue has already stretched until mid-August.
In Krasnoyarsk MVD it is impossible to obtain “for technical reasons”, without going into details, in the Samara region they honestly say that there are no forms, a similar situation is formed in other cities.
Many Muscovites have already encountered the problem, in social networks more and increasingly there are such messages:
Irina Burmistrova: “Cleague why you can not get international rights in Moscow?”
Correspond, because in all the departments of the traffic police ended forms.
Elena Podkolzina: "Questions to knowledgeable people!"
It is necessary to obtain international rights very urgently.
In Moscow is constantly clogged a long way forward, in the place of coupons do not betray at all (the button is there, but the coupon can not give).
It seems that the portal of public services shows that in Speb time is a free face.
Have you tried someone to get in a different city?
It's gonna work?
As explained in the Ministry of internal Affairs of the Russian Federation, the requirements for the forms of international driving certificates have changed, so new forms are supplied to the units of the State Traffic Inspectorate.
This may be associated with a deficit, however, it is unclear what changes we are talking about, it has not previously been reported.
Blanks are bought by the Special Purpose Center in the field of road traffic safety (CSN BDD) of the Ministry of internal Affairs of the Ministry of Internal Affairs of the RUSSIAN RF and then supplies them to the traffic police.
In recent years, all the contracts were concluded with Goznak JSC: in 2014-2015, almost 200 thousand membran forms were made, in 2016 15 thousand forms were purchased, in 2017 - 90 thousand, but the last contract was concluded on July 18 with LLC "Prince Pilutary" for the manufacture of 70 thousand forms.
There is a version that CSN simply did not have time to hold a tender on time, because of which there was a shortage.
However, there are other versions of the shortage of forms: because of the crisis, many people began to travel independently not to Europe, but to cheaper Asian countries - China, Thailand and so on.
What rights are accepted there, it is completely unclear, so people are insured, so there is an excitable demand for international “crusts”.
Recently it became known that professional drivers will have to take an exam for confirmation of their qualifications.
Such a proposal was made by the Ministry of Transport.
The International Driving Persuadence (IIA) of a new sample has been in effect since May 31, 2011.
The Minister of justice of Ukraine refused to believe in the construction of the Krymsky bridge
The Minister of justice of Ukraine Pavel Petrenko said that he does not believe in the ability of Russia to build a bridge in the Crimea.
About it on Friday, August 4, he said in an interview portal “Columnist”.
Not a self-respecting international company will even put a bomber or a wrench there, because it runs the risk of losing its business on the territory of the EU, the United States, Japan - in countries that have acceded to sanctions against Russia relative to the Crimea.
“That is, in my deep conviction, the prospects for this project actually does not exist,” Petrenko said.
He added that he believes Russia is incapacitated to implement a large infrastructure project on its own.
Russia can not normally build less large-scale facilities.
I know that after the Olympiad in Sochi, entire stadiums have already begun to break down.
“Therefore, I believe, the best tool in this situation is sanctions against companies that turned out to be so short-seaworthy to join this project”, – said the official. ”the official said.
on July 31, the builders completed the construction of a vault of the automobile arch of the Crimean Bridge.
On the Kerch coast, an enlarged assembly of the road arch of the Krymsky Bridge has been completed: its vault is enclosed at an altitude of 45 meter from the base of the structure.
“At the same time, bridge builders have been prepared for the installation on fairweather pillars of the railway arch”, – said in the information center of the project.
In April, the President of the Ministry of transport Maxim Sokolov informed the President of Russia Vladimir Putin that the construction of the object is ahead of schedule.
The Crimean bridge will connect the Crimean Peninsula and the Krasnodar Territory.
In Spain, fired an official who did not go to work for 10 years
What an angelial patience (or absolute indifference to civil service) should the head of the Spanish official Carles Recio have?
Absorption stretched for 10 long years.
However, Mr. Resio was still fired.
It’s not his immediate boss.
What does not happen in the bureaucratic world.
Inhabitants, it seems, have long been accustomed to all papples "servers of the people."
And, nevertheless, the officials are always able to impress those on whose taxes they live quite badly.
This time "sensation" came from Spain.
There, Valencia archive employee Carles Recio managed not to go to work for ten years for ten years.
At the same time, he regularly received a salary.
And the whole solid - 50 thousand euros a year.
And here the “miraculous times” of Mr. Resio is over.
He was dismissed according to the ruling assembly of Valencia.
During the investigation, it turned it out that a nervous walker every working morning came to the office at 07:00 to be noted in an electronic system.
Immediately he went home.
Once again he appeared in the workplace at 16:00, in order to again be noted in the system that he was gone.
That's 10 years.
It also became known that all his spare time the walker was dedicated to drawing comics at home.
Now the deputies of the legislative assembly of Valencia are thinking about how to punish the immediate superior of Mr. Recio, who could not fail to know how to “arbitrarificially work” in his workplace his subordinate.
Judgments Prohibited to Protect Against the President
The Presidential Council for human rights (HRC) on behalf of Vladimir Putin has developed proposals to strengthen the independence of the jurisprudence.
The HRC proposes to limit the powers of the chairmen of the courts and introduce their choice.
For courts of appellate and cassation, the HRC wants to introduce special constituencies, which will not be tied to the administrative-territorial division in the Russian Federation.
Its proposals within the framework of the presidential instruction should also be presented by the Supreme Court.
The HRC has completed the development of proposals, which will allow to strengthen the independence of Russian justice.
This work was carried out by the HRC on the instructions of Vladimir Putin dated January 3, 2017, which the President gave after a meeting with the members of the council.
At a meeting with the members of the council on December 8, 2016, individual cases of judicial arbitrariness were discussed, as well as the problems of public scrutiny in the detention of citizens (see "Kommersant" of December 9).
The work of the HRC consisted of 25 proposals, which deal both to ensure the independence of the judges and the identification of judicial errors, and the financing of courts and legal education.
One of the ideas of the Kremlin human rights defenders is to limit the powers of the chairmen of the courts to increase the independence of other judges.
If the candidate for the position of a judge successfully passed the competition and received the support of the judicial community, then the head of the court, in the opinion of the HRC, must submit him to the appointment, not having the right to refuse, as the law now allows.
It is also proposed to deprive the chairman of the right to allocate cases for consideration among the judges.
To do this, the experts allow, a specially written computer program can do.
It is also in the HRC that the Chairman does not have the right to “determine predetermine the results of the qualification appraisal of a judge, to initiate his bringing to disciplinary responsibility, to make decisions on the establishment of additional material payments”.
At the same time, the presidential Council considers it necessary to move to the “electorate of the chairmen of the courts by the judges themselves” and “encourage their powers for a relatively short period with mandatory rotation”.
Now all the presidences of the courts (from the republican to district) are appointed for a six-year-old president on the proposal of the Chairman of the Supreme Court of the Russian Federation.
In order to protect the judges from the pressure of regional administrations, the HRC proposes in a new manner to organize an appeal and cassation in the courts of general jurisdiction.
Now their structure is tied to the administrative-territorial division in the Russian Federation.
The HRC says that "it is Necessary to ensure the organization of certain courts of appellate and cassation bodies not at the level of regional judicial bodies in the subjects of the Russian Federation, but in judicial districts."
Experts take as a basis the jurisprudence of arbitrator courts.
With them there are “judicial constituencies”, which do not coincide with the administrative division in the Russian Federation, but thus guarantee greater independence from regional officials who are difficult to use “telephone rights”.
NCHR proposes to strengthen world justice judges in order to consider certain “categories of civil and administrative cases” with their participation.
For example, on the deprivation of parental entourage, about reinstatement at work, about the protection of honor and dignity, on the deprivation of a driver's license, etc.
“These are only our proposals”, – told “Kommersant” a member of the HRC, a judge of the Constitutional court in the retired Tamara Morshchychak.
She also reminded that the instructions of the President applied not only to the HRC, but also to the Supreme Jurisprudence, which has not yet disclosed its proposals.
There is still a time for fulfilling the instructions of the Armed Forces (among co-pleasants - the General Prosecutor's Office and the Commissioner for human rights in the Russian Federation).
To report to Vladimir Putin on how effectively the independence of the state of justice is ensured in the Russian Federation, Vyacheslav Lebedev owes until September 1.
To live a high life: the semi-floor and cunning design techniques turned this small apartment in Earles Cort into a spacious dwelling
Joan Lee, a former banker advocivating for renovating real estate, in 2014 moved from a spacious house in Knightsbridge to an apartment in Earls Cort.
The apartment is located on the first-floor of a pretty typical Queen Anne-style house, and in favor of the new design says that Joan did not collect her belongings and did not move again.
“Before, I was living with my former in Nytzbridge in a much larger area,” says Joan.
“I was looking for something comparable for my money.
They showed me this apartment in Earls Cort, and here there were the same high ceilings.
I fell in in love with her and offered the price on the same day.”
From the moment of the first browsing the apartment with an area of 1000-square-floors has undergone a complete refurbishment.
Initially, it was an apartment with a one-difficulty bedroom layout - in order to get into the bedroom, you had to pass through the kitchen - and Joanna wanted to add space for storing things and a semi-floor-floor to squeeze the maximum benefit from the genitous height of the ceiling.
"I wanted high ceilings, large windows, a lot of light.
“That’s what were my demands,” she said.
To this end, she hired Erfane Azadi from the Netting-Hill architectural and design studio Duck & Shed to use 12.5 ft-hundred-height ceilings and created a dwelling that would not only be a successful project, but Joan would be suitable for life.
The Ceiling wasn't tall enough to arrange two rooms above the other, so the architectural task was to create a semi-floor room where it would be possible to stand at full height.
Erfanov had to think creatively to cope with a brief.
“Work with steel structures is very difficult,” he explains.
“We had to arrange the premises so that they were one above the other and did not have to bending.
It was necessary not just to build a simple platform, but to bend the structures so that they were at the right height and allow the use of the premises from above and from the bottom.”
This solution allowed Erfanov to arrange two full-simplate rooms one above the other in the allotted space - and a lot more interesting.
From the semi-floor through the vintage copper light window from "Retrouvius" there is a view of a chic living room at the bottom.
Mirror furnipotrian furniture with golden decoration, silver accents and vintage lighting devices from Serge Muya specify the style of the project.
Mirror use plays a role in the addition of spectacle, spaciousness and light.
A short corridor is floated with mirrors so that it may seem longer.
In the Kitchen, the Mirror Shielding Panel looks like a window to the other room.
Mirror wardrobes serve to store all Joan utensils.
To create the feeling of a more luxurious space, the beauty of the living room can block the kitchen when it is not used.
There’s nothing going to be new about kitchens.
the uniqueness of this kitchen is that it is a moving door, just like in a garage.
"Engistor art was involved here," Erfan tells about a reinforced steel-fighted shield door.
“It is equipped with a counterbalancing, so when you push the door up, it slides very easily.”
Thanks to the sensible use of space and storage space, Joan received an additional 16-square meter, an additional bedroom and an improved layout.
“At the end of the day, the area of the sex is exactly what you’re going to sell, that’s what your real estate is being valued,” Erfan said.
Roughly speaking, the real estate agent will come in and will make calculations on the basis of the area of the floors.
Here they were able to enlarge the area of the floors, using high-quality materials that give the space a shade of luxury.
“Materials are what we touch, so they help create an sociable connection with the house,” Erfan says.
"No one falls in love with electrical wiring in the walls.
It’s important, but doesn’t touch the strings of our hearts.”
This serves as a testimonial to the fact that due to a good design and enlarged meter, an apartment can turn into something terrific.
In fact, just like Joan, you can decide to stay.
The government approved the creation of a commission on cultural policy
The government of Russia approved the creation of a commission on issues of state cultural policy.
Corresponding decree is published on the government website.
According to the document, the main task of the commission will be the development and adjustment of strategic approaches to the implementation of cultural policy.
Also, the Commission will also develop draft strategies of cultural policy, clarify tasks and prepare new programs for its implementation.
The Deputy Chairman of the Government of the Russian Federation was appointed the head of the commission.
The composition of the commission will be approved separately.
The Prime Minister of the Russian Federation Dmitry Medvedev in 2016 approved a plan for the implementation strategy of the state cultural policy until 2030.
The plan includes 193 events and envisages measures to expand the influence of Russian culture in other countries, the preservation of a common cultural space and cultural heritage, it will also contribute to the creation of conditions for the development of culture in the country.
Inflation in the G20 decreased to an eight-Yo-Yo-Year
The growth of consumer prices in the G20 countries has decreased to a minimum over the last eight years, reports The Wall Street Journal, citing data from the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD).
According to OECD estimates, inflation in June of 2016 amounted to 2% - lower values were observed in October 2009, when the price growth index reached 1.7%.
Earlier, Rosstat reported a 0.1% decrease in the consumer price index in Russia by 0.1%.
Thus, the Agency recorded the first weekly deflation in 2017.
Inflation target in Russia, according to the calculations of the Ministry of Finance, is 4.1%.
The Ministry of Economial, however, believes that the target value has already been achieved - according to this department, the figure is 4%.
“Putin warned against illegal deforestation Baikal taiga
The Russian leader Vladimir Putin during a meeting on the environmental development of the Baikal territory warned against the illegal destruction of forests.
In the course of the event, the Minister of Natural Resource Sergey Donskoy noted that a bill was previously prepared.
It allows deforestation during the liquidation of the fires, and the government plans to accept it in the autumn.
In turn, the President said that this project it is necessary to ensure that in the process of deforestation “everything will not be knocked down”.
Donskoy noted that this bill assumes control from the Emergencies Ministry and supervisory authorities.
Media: the soldiers of the AFU in secret from the command agree with the militia of the Donbass
On the line of the armed confrontation in the Dordinations in the Donbass, regular telephone communication has been established.
Soldiers of the opposing sides are constantly communicating with each other on mobile phones, and they don’t even know communication about it at the headquarters.
Fighters of the AFU and Militants of the Donbaps established communal communication on cell phones in secret from their high command.
About it on August 4 reports “Strana.ua” with reference to the participants of the military operation in the Donbass.
According to the publication, the commanders of the units perfectly know the names of their colleagues on the opposite side of the front and daily communicate with them by phone.
Communication is not at all household: the commanders are trying to reach certain “tactical agreements”.
Often, according to the results of such conversations is a truce on a certain part of the front.
Journalists became aware of the cases when congratulations on the birthday of one or another the officer received because of the front line, from his formal enemy.
The soldiers of the Armed Forces of the Armed Forces of the Armed Forces of the DPR and LPR are sitting in the trenches on the demarcation line from the spring of 2014, when Ukraine launched a combat operation against the Donbass.
The foreign Ministry was indignant about the blocking the statements of the UN security Council on attacks on the Russian Embassy
The Russian foreign Ministry is indignant about the actions of certain Western diplomatic representatives, who are blocking the statements of the UN Security Council in the press, condemning the terrorist attacks of the Russian Embassy in Syria.
This is reported by the Russian foreign Ministry.
The Ministry reminded that the territory of the Russian Embassy in Damascus for the third time in a month was mortaquely shelled by the terrorists of Hayat Tahrir al-Sham (the former Jabhat al-Nusra, banned in the Russian Federation) and Failak al-Rahman.
Taking into account the fact that the international community unanimously in the qualification of “Nusra” as a terrorist organization, and UN Security Council resolutions call to oppose this structure, the Russian foreign Ministry noted that “it would, of course, that Necessarily, Nusra terrorist attacks should meet a universal unconditional and resolute condemnation, and there should be no ambiguity in the estimates of sorties against diplomatic missions”.
However, as noted in the diplomatic department, “already for the third time in a month, the diplomatic representatives of the United States, Great Britain, France and Ukraine in the UN Security Council, alternately, varying the tonality of objections, hiding behind arguments about the alleged absence of the necessary information, blockaded the proposal of the Russian Federation to accept a standard short draft statement of the Security Council for the press condemning the terrorist attacks on the Russian diplomatic mission in the Syrian capital.
Reluctance to show diplomatic souquetes with us to remain on the conscience of these delegations.
“It’s most reckless that the inability of the Security Council to denounce the actions of terrorists encourages them to new provocations and terrorist attacks, gives them a sense of impunity”, – said the foreign ministry and added that “we would not like these barbarians to create the belief that someone in the Security Council with them at the same time.”
Vladimir Putin called for the restriction of the number of unscheduled business checks
Russian President Vladimir Putin during the meeting on investment projects in the Far East said that the number of unscheduled inspections of entrepreneurs should be reduced to 30% from the number of plans, and also spoke about the need to limit the timing of inspections to ten days.
“Unscheduled inspections are carried out, as a rule, without proper coordination with the Prosecutor’s office; only 2-3% is coordinated with the Prosecutor’s office, everything else goes on its own”, – quotes the President of TASS.
Volodymyvdon Putin also said that it is necessary to prohibit investigators to seize servers and hard drives in enterprises.
In addition, according to the President, business associations should receive the right to protect the interests of their members in court.
“I, I hope, will introduce a certain positivity into the consideration of cases related to entrepreneurial activity, or related to the violation of the law in the field of entrepreneurship,” the head of state said.
According to Kommersant, due to a moratorium on scheduled checks, the number of other types of inspections of entrepreneurs is growing.
In May at the request of the business ombudsman under the President of Russia Boris Titov will conduct a survey, as a result of which it turned out that in fact there was a replacement of scheduled inspections unscheduled (the share faced with them increased from 21.9% in 2015 to 30.8% in 2016), procuratorial (from 16.9% to 21.8%), traffic jams (from 7.9% to 13.3%), as well as checks on the applications of citizens (an increase from 15%).
Read more about business checks in Kommersant material "Monthly business went from the other side to small business."
Broughts fighting for a real estate empire worth more than $ 500 million
Two of the brothers are at war for one of Victoria’s largest real estate-profficiencies worth more than $500 million – forty-three years after their Italian forerunners founded a dynasty dynasty.
The former director of the football club Carleton and the developer Colin de Luthyce lives in the Palace of Turak through three doors from his younger brromrum Paul, who filed a lawsuit against the Supreme Judgment about the division of possession and assets.
Paul wants to withdraw from the family business since 2014, but in the Verkhovna court there is a fierce dispute about the conditions of the divorce.
Together with her mother, Anne’s brothers have owned more than half a billion-dollar objects purchased since their family bought a Smith-Street store at Collingwood in 1973.
There, the family founded Westco Jeans, which grew into a network of 160 retail outlets.
It was sold for $85 million in 1999.
The money was invested in the real estate, and the list of possessions of the De Luthis family includes today office buildings, buildings in Brunswik and Sorrrento, apartments on the Golden Shore and Mount Boueller and shopping machinations in the suburbs.
By agreement with the deceased father, Kolynn - whom Paul describes as "the principal driving force and dominant personality" of the De Lyutis family - owns about two-three-three of the company's assets, and Paul holds about one-and-a-three.
According to the court, this means that Kollin’s property is 316 million, and Pola - 176 million.
Separation of property and money has become a stumbling stool for Paul.
“The section Promoted by Kolin gives him, in my opinion, the best parts of the property”, – he wrote in his first testimony in 2015.
Last Friday after several unsuccessful conciliation attempts took place the first hearing in the Verkhovna court.
The brothers are now arguing about who will control the existing business - from which, according to Paul, Kolin excluded him.
Kolylin claims that this is not the case, but accuses Paul of incompetent management of certain facilities.
According to Kolin’s testimony at the beginning of the process, he says he hopes to resolve the dispute.
“My Italian roots make me consider the family the highest priority,” he wrote.
Judgment costs are growing as a snowball: Hundreds of pages of testimonies, e-mails and reports of companies such as Deloitte, Pitcher Partners and Charter Keck Cramer are attached; both parties have attracted the most famous lawyers, including the royal lawyer Allan Meyers, and the best strollers.
Mr. De Luthies and her late husband Luigi were immigrants from Italy; since the late 1950-ies they controlled dairy bars and gastronomies, and in the early 1970's bought a store in Brunswick.
Under financial guarantees, they bought a store in Collingwood, in which Kollin opened the first family jeans store.
Kolyn says that he launched Westco, when he was "in the last classes of the school, and Paul was then a boy (approximately 10 years old)".
Anne De Lütis says that he and Luigi, who died in 2012, had hoped to transfer their possessions to their sons without conflict.
“Luige often told me he didn’t want the brethren to figure it in court,” she wrote.
Two other similates, Mark and Luke, are no longer part of De Luthyce; Colina says that Mark received 10 million when he went out of business and Luke 26 million.
According to Paul, both Luke and Mark were "dissatisfied with the financial conditions of his office."
Kolynon was not a public figure, although he was a former member of the board of directors of the AFL and, according to a biography of Eddie McGuire published in 2015.
"Ferfax Media" on Friday contacted Colin and Paul with their lawyers.
Kolyn replied, with a text message, which said that since the case has not yet been considered in court, “I don’t really have much to say.”
“I very, very much deplore that my brute brother Paul decided to sue me and renundier the name of our family in court,” he wrote.
In the middle of 2016, Kolyin wrote in the testimony that he was trying to satisfy his brother's demands.
“Our father doesn’t want to see Paul and I arrguing in court in court,” he said, adding that “it’s still looking forward to resolve the conflict.”
On Friday, this hope seemed to dissipate.
“The decision in our case will soon be handed down by the court,” Kolyn wrote.
The new head of the office of trump plans to limit the flow of information to the President.
Others tried to do this and were defeated.
Maybe John F. Kelly will really succeed.
In this case, he will be the first.
“Political” reports that the new head of the White house office plans to limit the flow of information coming to the President of trump, including news reports from the media – hoping to keep the chef in a calmer state.
That's what reporter Josh Daws reports.
“At the meeting, which was convened by the new head of the White house John F. Kelly with the management of the device on his first working day, he outlined the main problem in the White House under President Donald trump, whom he hopes to decide: the bad channels of receiving information to the President.”
Kelly told employees that the information should pass through it - in a paper form or through briefings - because the president will be better to make decisions if he receives the right information.
Kelly’s diagnosis is quite correct, but others have already failed, trying to pacify trump, tracking the receipt of information to him.
President trump’s relations with television took place a few decades ago – and now that he’s at the White House, his habit of watching TV is still strong.
“When trump, as a candidate, resented the unjust coverage of the campaign, it was useful to demonstrate to him that he was receiving fair coverage in publications that could have been persuaded,” Sam Nanberg, a former adviser to the election headquarters, told Politico in February.
Tara Palméri then wrote in Politico that "according to the six former members of the election headquarters, in order to certify trump's habit of writing on Twitter, it was necessary to ensure a constant flow of praise in coming to him personally."
All right.
But the premise that Trump’s habit of tweeting has ever been “guided” is simply ridiculous.
“Maybe these campaign members know something we don’t know—such as it weren’t for them, Trump’s tweets more provocative.
We may never find out about the tweet that Trump hasn’t published.
If its employees saved him from trouble at least several times, their efforts were not in vain.
But no one has always managed to keep trump from sticking fuel to the fire.
Part of the problem lies the fact that in the White House, divided into gambling factions, people are constantly trying to promote their subpoena by submitting material - reliable or not - which confirms their views.
"Politico" - just to this story - wrote in May about the inclination of advisers to continually conceit to the president dubious information.
Here’s one example described by reporter Shane Goldmacher:
“Turdish and former Trump officials say that trump can react very sharply to negative reports in the press, especially those containing dangerous leaks of information and will not rest until he finds who was behind them.
So it happened at the end of last February, when someone slipped to the president an imminent release of an article with GotNews.com, the website of the Internet pro-provocator Charles K. Johnson, in which the deputy head of the apparatus Katie Welsh was accused of being “behind nearby leaks” in the White house.
It doesn’t matter that Johnson is forever banned on Twitter for aggressive behavior, that he didn’t present specific facts or that in the past he launched false accusations and then renounced them.
Trump read the article and began to ask employees about Welsh."
Goldmaker adds that the then Chief of Staff Raines Priebus and Secretary Rob Porter "tried to build a system to control the flow of the securities that Trump receives and to document them."
How'd it work?
Three Months later, Kelly tries to do the same.
Perhaps he will prove to be a more effective manager than Priebus, but trump is still impulsive nature, and his assistants are still fighting each other for influence.
These Continuing Factors make Kelly’s task very not easy.
The Tyumen Prosecutor's office is struggling with an HIV dissident
The Prosecutor’s office contested the decision of the Kalininsky district court of Tyumen, who terminated a criminal case against a local resident, whose young daughter died from HIV.
According to the investigation, the child died due to the fact that the mother is an HIV-dissident and refused treatment.
However, the court released her from responsibility in connection with reconciliation with the injured father.
The Prosecutor’s office believes that the crime can not be left unpunished, so as not to create a precedent for other HIV dissidents.
The case against a resident of Tyumen was instituted under Part 1 of article 109 of the criminal code of the Russian Federation (causing death by negligence) in April - after her three-year-old's daughter died from HIV-influence.
According to the Prosecutor’s office, the mother herself is HIV-influenced.
“The woman was not treated by herself and refused the treatment of her daughter, believing that an HIV infection does not exist”, – stated in the Prosecutor’s office of the Tyumen region.
The criminal case was received by the Kalininsky district court of Tyumen, which on July 25 made a decision on its termination.
The petition was filed by the father of the deceased girl, explaining that “forgained his wife, has no claims to her, she made up the harm and apologized”.
The prosecutor's office did not agree with the court's decision and filed an appeal, demanding to repeal the decision on the termination of the case and forward it for a new consideration.
The girl died, and it is impossible to make amends for the harm caused by a crime.
The HIV-infected mother, contrary to the recommendations of the doctors, refused to examine the baby and the treatment of her from a dangerous infection, ”the press service of the prosecutor’s office said.
According to the Supervisory authority, it should be punished, otherwise other HIV dissidents will follow suit.
As told in the Tyumen AIDS Center, now in the Tyumen region there are about 12 children with HIV do not receive medical care due to the refusal of their parents.
“And this situation has already been improved - over a year of the work of a special group, half of parents who categorically refused to treat children from HIV have changed their mind - they allowed to carry out a diagnosis, they began to take the drugs", - said the press Secretary of the AIDS Center Elena Loseva.
According to her, it is not possible to influence their parents in a legislative way, and as a result, it is possible to detect all HIV-infected children - the mothers do not allow them to be examined, hiding, running away with children from hospitals.
What is the Danger of HIV Dissidents
at the end of last year St. Petersburg sociologists presented the results of the first in Russia study of the so-called movement of HIV-dissidents.
HIV-dissipidents call people who denies the existence of HIV and refuse to take medication.
Physicians and entourages of AIDS-service NGOs call such views anti-medical, and in their ciquappation they see a serious threat.
Terrible photo shoot, which ended with a tragedy, occurred on Thursday, August 3, at the railway station in Khmelnytsky.
A cheerful company of drinking young people walked the bridge over the railway, where the freight train just stood.
One of the friends had the idea to take a spectacular slephie on the root of the car, told “FACTS” in the communication sector of police in the Khmelnytskyi region.
The guy began to descend from the bridge to the train, but due to its negligence, he clings to the power line and instantly received an electric shock.
Luckily, about this case it became known to the dispatcher of the station, who immediately summoned an “emergency”.
Before the arbitrarily, the victim’s doctors were moved to a safe place, and then he was hospitalized in the Burning Department of the Khmelnytsky Regional Clinical Hospital.
The man was diagned the touring burns of 1-2 dens.
Now his condition is evaluated by the doctors as stable.
Law enforcers remind that in recent years, extreme selves are becoming increasingly popular on the roofs of high-rhistance buildings, bridges, moving transport.
The police are urging people to be vigilant and do not allow such photoshoals, especially among children and teenagers.
Scholars allowed the existence of the oceans on ancient Venus
On ancient Venus there could be oceans.
This assumption was made by French scientists.
Experts have created a computer model, which demonstrated the formation of water on the surface of the planets, writes Science News.
It turned out that on Venus at the beginning of its history there were oceans, in which there was 10% more water than now on Earth.
Arguments of the Week previously wrote that, according to the hypothesis of scientists, the ocean 4 billion years ago could have existed on Mars.
Foreign specialists in the course of their research came to the conclusion that the water object was located on the northern hemisphere of the Red Planet.
As a result of the shooting in a park in San Francisco, three people were injured
In San Francisco as a result of the shooting, three people were injured, reports the Associated Press.
