The rock band Louna will unveil in Barnaul a new Album
Louna’s concert will take place in Barnaul on October 7.
The musicians will present their new Album “Wonder New World”, which became one of the most anticipated releases of the year.
The group prepares a conceptual show, which will be the brightest in the concert history of the group.
"Waid new world" - the fourth album of the Russian rock band Louna.
Its name is connected with the well-known dystopian dystopia of Hucksley “On a Brave New World”.
New songs do not respel the book, but talk about a society that lives according to the law of dystopia “blind believing propaganda and imposed values”.
To collect money to the recording of the album, the group was assisted by listeners: more than 1200 people supported the project on the website "Planeta.ru".
Louna released her first album "Take Louder!" Louna was released in 2010.
Two-Yad-on-half, the musicians unveiled “Time X”, and in 2013 they recorded the album “We are Louna” (2013).
In the autumn of 2015, Louna performed a symphony orchestra at Crocus City Hole with the program “Song of the World”.
As part of the group of Lusine Gevorkyan (vocal), Vitaly Demidenko (bass-gital), Reuben Ghazaryan (guitar), Sergey Ponkratiev (guitara), Leonid Kinzbursky (dumbrates).
The concert will be held in the Barnaul club "Pharaon" on October 17 at 19.00.
The price of tickets: from 1200 to 2600 rubles.
Louna - one of the demanded groups on the Russian rock stage.
The group was founded in 2008.
Their debut concert took place in 2009.
The group several times has won in different nominations "Devil Dozen".
Gypsies overcame the moat and returned to the “millionaire street”
Some of West’s wealthiest homeowners are again in conflict with responsive gypsies who overcame moats duggled by the municipal authorities to reoccupy the field next to their homes.
Gypsies parked 20 houses on wheels in the field, bordering the rich street Soligalla, which received the jokingly name “millionaire street”.
Bleaving horses, infants, and a lot of Wheels houses, they returned after they were kicked out no further than in May and they did not interfere with moats dug by the municipal authorities to prevent their intrusion.
This tactful company found a rupture in the defensive structures and squeezed its vehicles through a site that was left unencumbered in order to leave room for the trail.
Angry residents attacked the municipality of Solikhalla, saying that he was “incapable of solving this problem”.
An animated local resident reported: “They came here on Monday evening, after being chased by Bentley Heath where they threw stones at passers-by.”
Muncipality should be shamed and forced to act, because they are completely incapable of solving this problem.
The gypsies were here in May, they were chased, and here they come back again.
Last night there were even more gypsies, and today, perhaps even more.
“Birmingham municipality knows how to solve this problem, they receive long-term court orders to protect their parks,” she added.
“I’m living on Stretsbrook Road, and I don’t like that I’m still paying a municipal tax and the municipality can’t even put an end to it.”
“It’s funny, a local resident who wished to remain annointed: “It’s funny, we’ve just seen these gypsies leave the last time, and here, please, this attack is going on.”
This time there were more of them, and we even saw a horse groving in a meadow.”
A spokeswoman for Solihalla said: "We are aware of an illegal camp on the ground near Stretsbruck Rod and are collaborating with Solihull police; we are taking the necessary legal action in order as soon as possible."
To assist us in collecting the testimonies, it is very important that as many locals as possible report any anti-Social or criminal behavior to the police by phone.
This allows you to obtain an idea of the situation that will be considered by the court when we present our case.
Crimea emplifies the champagne riot plant “New World”
SUE of the Republic of the Crimea "Champagne vinition plant "New Svet" decided to corporatize, transforming to OJSC Champagne Wine Factory "New Svet", it follows from the order of the Minister of property and land relations of the Crimea Anne Anyukhina.
100% of the shares of the enterprise will remain in the state property of the Crimea.
The authorized capital of the joint-stock company will amount to 595.5 million rub. and it will consist of 5.955 million ordinary shares with a porous value of 100 rubles each.
The Ministry of agriculture of the Crimea stated that if within the next three years there will be no funds for the modernization of the enterprise, there will be a threat of stopping the plant.
Depreciation of fixed-end funds in the enterprise is about 60-70%.
For the modernization of the enterprise it is Necessary 1.2 Billion Rubles. Due to the peculiarities of the organizational and legal form, it is obliged to give 50% of the profit to the budget income.
What remains remains is not enough for the implementation of the modernization plan.
Receiving money from the owner is problematic, it is more difficult to talk about attracting borrowed funds of large credit institutions,” – said the deputy head of the Ministry of agriculture of the Crimea Sergey Petelin in April of this year.
The Parliament of the Crimea included the enterprise in the forecast plan of privatization for 2017
It was proposed to corporatize it and put it up for auction.
The source of “Interfax” in the authorities of the Crimea estimated the possible cost of selling the enterprise at $ 40 million, the investor’s investments in the modernization of another $ 30 million.
"New Light" in 2016 increased the production of sparkling riots by 2.8% compared to the level of 2015 - to 1.52 million bottles.
In 2017, "New Svet" intended to produce 1.6 million bottles.
The plant was founded in 1878 by Prince Lion Golitsyn as a plant for the production of sparkling wine in the New Svet estate acquired by him.
The plant is located on 11 hectare of land.
Nizhny Novgorod third-graders defeated more than 40 tombstone
Employees of the Ministry of internal Affairs in the Nizhny Novgorod region have established the identities of citizens who destroyed 46 tombstones in the cemetery of the city of Lyskovo.
Involuntescrenants were third-class disciples.
The first statement that the tomb stove is damaged by unknown persons was received by the OMVD of Russia in the Lylovsky district on June 27.
In total, 24 people appealed to the police about this.
As a result, a criminal case was initiated under article 244 of the criminal code “Destruction, Damage or desecration of burial sites”.
Based on the results of the investigation, the police identified the suspects, they turned out to be two schoolchildren at the age of 8 and 9.
Juvenile offenders told the police that they were interested to see how the monuments were falling, this prompted them to hooligan actions.
preventive measures were carried out with their children and their parents.
“Italy tightens the tone in relation to the ships of NGOs saving migrants.
Italy has wardened an NGO that owns rescue ships in the Mediterranean that they would not be able to continue their work if they did not comply with the new rules governing their operations.
“Unless the NGO obeys a new code of conduct, it is difficult to say whether they will be able to continue their activities,” Interior Minister Mario Minniti said in an interview with the Turin daily Stamp newspaper.
Minniti’s warning came just day after Italian authorities confiscated a ship belonging to the German humanitarian organization Jugend Rette on suspicion that its crew was actually collaborating with human traffickers and facilitating illegal immigration.
The humanitarian organization, which lasted only a year, refused to comment on the mere detailed accusations brought against it by the Italian prosecutor Ambrogjo Cartosio.
“For us to save human life is and will remain the highest priority, so we very much sorry that we can not now continue to work in the zone of search and salvation”, – reads the organization’s statement in social networks.
“We will be able to evaluate all the accusations made now, only after we collect all the information and will be able to assess the situation.”
The Italian authorities have been following Juwenta’s Juventa, owned by Jugend Rette, since October.
Its crew is accustomed to the fact that whole lifeboats took on board the migrants who traffickers sent directly to them and allowed the smugglers to leave along with the boats, which they could use again.
At least one such meeting, as expected, took place only 1.3 mile from the Libyan coast - this is according to the accusation, whose contents were published in the Italian media.
The crew is suspected of infringing the regulations of the Italian coastal authorities, who control rescue operations in this area, rather from humanitarian vouring than for any other motive.
The code of conduct presupègs, mainly that Juventa-type vessels will have on board an Italian police officer who will monitor their activities.
While only three of the nine NGOs participating in search and rescue operations have agreed to obey the code: “Sysweet the Children”, the Maltese MOAS and “Pro-Activa Dispersed hugs” from Spain.
The Latter Said on Thursday she considers the new rules unnecessary, but acceptable on the condition that they do not entail “significant changes or hurdles” to her rescue operations.
Among those who refused to sign, there is a Nobel Prize-paternity organization “Doctors without Borders” (MSF).
In the mean meantime, Minniti said a sharp decline in recent weeks in recent weeks on the number of migrants arriving in Italy as a result of rescue operations indicates that efforts to support the Libyan coast guard and co-operation with local mayors are bearing fruit.
“In the last few days, we’ve begun to see light at the end of the tunnel,” the minister said.
He announced plans for further negotiations with Libyan mayors on initiatives for economic development and with Chad, Niger and Mali about measures to reduce the number of migrants leaving those countries in the hope of reaching Europe.
“We don’t want to be associated with any of the parties to the conflict.”
The authorities of the Russian Federation have recently noticeably activated their policy in the Libyan direction, and with visits to Moscow, delegations of the opposing Libyan parties have vacated.
The head of the Russian contact group on an intra-Libyan settlement under the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Federation and the state Duma, the assistant to the head of the Chechen Republic Lev Deva told Kommersant what the goals of Moscow in this region pursues in this region.
There’s almost nothing is known about the contact group on Libya that you’re leading.
Here, let’s say, the contact group in Ukraine – everyone is aware of it.
And here's a veil of secrecy.
What exactly do you deal with, what goals do you pursue?
The contact group was created at the initiative of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Federation and the State Duma.
Its activities are supervised by Deputy Foreign Minister Mikhail Bogdanov and Adam Delimkhanov (Deputy of the Duma from Chechnya. - Kommersant).
The latter is authorised to work in the Libyan direction by the speaker of the state Duma Vyacheslav Volodin.
The impetus for the creation of the group was the detention in Libya of the Russian tanker "Mekhaynik Chebotarev" (in September 2015, on board there were 11 people - "Kommersant").
We were wondering about how to help the crew.
Then a contact group was created from military specialists, representatives of the state Duma, our work was supported by the head of Chechnya Ramzan Kadyrov.
And how did it turn out that it was you who headed it?
Since I have been working on Libya since 2008, I was approached with a proposal to lead the work of the group.
Our work was not limited to the liberation of sailors from Mechanika Chebotarev.
We managed to establish contacts with representatives of all the main groups opposed to each other in the Libyan-Luvical conflict - and from Tripoli (where the UN-recognized government is founded, headed by Faiz Sarraj - "Kommersant"), and Tobruk (residence of parliament, which opposes the government and supports Marshal Khalif Haftara, who oversees the eastern regions of Libya - Komm).
Thanks to the active participation of Ahmed Metig (Deputy Premier of Libya – “Kommersant”), we quickly managed to reach an agreement on the releasing Russian sailors.
Then it was decided in order to more effectively use these contacts, to create a contact group.
Its task is to analyze the situation, the identification of key factors and players, the dialogue with all the parties to the conflict.
I want to emphasize that in Libya we do not want to be associated against any of the parties to the conflict, we are conducting a dialogue with everyone.
how many people are included in the contact group and how many of them are constantly located in Libya?
Now the contact group includes five people.
Among them, there are people who have experience working in law enforcement agencies, including the Ministry of Defense.
We also want to introduce a group of specialists in the region, representatives of the Institute of the Middle East of the RUSSIAN RAS.
No one is constantly in Libya of our employees, there is not yet a need for this.
Are there currently Russian military advisers, instructors in Libya.
And if so, on whose side is it?
There are no Russian military specialists in Libya.
All conversations and publications are untrengageable.
But in your contact group, the former military enters ...
Yes, and their presence is necessary.
For example, when we are visiting hot spots.
Or such closed until a certain point for our cities as Misrata (where militia units are based, which played a role in the ousting of the Libyan leader Muammar Gaddafi in 2011 and noticeably intensified in the following years. - "Kommersant").
We came to Misrata this January.
We were freaked out, they said that there are all Islamists, terrorists at all.
But it was very important for us to assess the situation there ourselves, to analyze the real military potential who is responsible for something, why such rumors circulate, what the role of the Islamists is really there.
In Misrata we met with all representatives of the detachments that were engaged in the destruction of ISIS in Sirte (in December 2016 this city on the Mediterranean coast was recaptured from the militants banned in Russia “Islamic state” – “Kommersant”).
We wanted to look at them, to get acquainted with these people, to verify the information that they played a decisive role in the destruction of ISIS in Libya, and not Khalifa Haftar who attributed these melodies to themselves.
And to what conclusion did you come to?
“The “Islamic state” in Libya did not defeat Haftar?
He wasn't doing it.
Haftar carried out operations on the other front in Benghazi.
And ISIS in Sirte was tied by structures subordinated to the government in Tripoli.
And, by the way, we invited people to Russia who conducted this anti-terrorist operation.
And they arrived - the visit lasted from 19 to 23 April this year, the Libyan delegation was received in the Federation Council, in the Duma, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Regardie.
As far as we have understood, you are in all Libyan regions, and you’re probably conceiving the mood of local elites and warlords.
What do you do you think it will be possible to carry out the cease-to-piercing agreements, on the holding of an election, which was reached at the end of July by Khalifa Haftar and Faiz Sarraj?
Or again, as it has happened repeatedly in the past, the agreements will be thwarted, the fighting will resume, the parties will try to seize power alone?
For us a good signal has already become the fact that Saraj and Haftar agreed to the next meeting, not so long ago it was impossible.
In the recent past, the two leaders negatively responded negatively about each other.
As for the position of Russia...
They often write and say that Moscow actively supports Haftar, many people believe this.
We are faced with this situation, when we were in Misrata, and Haftar on this day rose on board the Russian aircraft carrier "Admiral Kuznetsov".
It was a coincidence.
But Misrata didn't believe in a coincidence.
We were told: "You're probably very courageous people who came to us today."
But our task is precisely to show that we do not only support Haftar, we are conducting a dialogue with all the key parties to the conflict in Libya.
You and Haftar communicated.
Does mutual understanding eased with Russian partners on the human and emotional level the fact that he twice studied in the USSR?
And, by the way, does Haftar know the Russian language?
If he's Russian, if he's a lot of it, it's a lot.
But the fact that he was learning from us, of course, facilitates the dialogue with him.
By the way, it’s not just with him.
When we communicate with the military in Tripoli and Misrata, we meet the generals who have studied either in Russia or still in the Soviet Union.
And here they speak very well in Russian.
And are drawn to Russia, to some extent experience nostalgic on it.
Do you think the imminentiary imminentially lifting of the arms embargo imposed on Libya?
Do your Libyan interlocutors are interested in the supply of Russian weapons?
Of course we are interested, but, as I have already said, we don't take sides in this conflict and we would not like to arm some to the detriment of others.
We would like everyone to be in roughly equal positions.
As for the arms embargo, there are constantly calls from the Libyans that Russia somehow contribute to its removal.
Now the process of drafting a constitution is actively progressing in Libya.
We hope that the parties will come to compromise solutions and reach an internal consensus.
Then there should be an election, as discussed at the meeting of Saraj and Haftar.
If the elections take place and will finally be elected a legitimate authority (and now none of the parties has such a status), then it is possible to put the issue of lifting the arms embargo in the UN Security Council.
To raise this issue now meaningless and dangerous, this will only lead to an escalation of the conflict.
Recently in the media there was information that Italy, faced with the problem floating African refugees from Libya, feels abandoned to the mercy of allies from the European Union.
Can Moscow in this situation help the Italian partners, using its ties with the Libyans?
How, for example, is it a realistic possibility that Haftar’s detachments will establish control of the coast and put an end to the business of smugglers transporting immigrants to Europe?
A very temporary question.
We are actively working on this.
The Italians are in need of the support of Russia, because Moscow conducts a dialogue at the same time with Haphtar, Sarraj, Misrata and the south of the country.
And in this matter, tribes in southern Libya play an important role, and they are ready to cooperate with Russia.
We're talking about making southerners stop the flow of migrants on long-distance approaches?
That is, conditionally speaking, unplundered back the buses in which Nigerian migrants go?
We're looking forward to it.
But it's not easy.
Some crannies and groups have an interest in ensuring that these streams continue.
We hope to help unite the southerners in the negotiation process between Saraj, Haftar and tribes in the south.
But for a start, we would like to see a unity of opinion on this issue between Haftar and Sarraj.
The head of the government in Tripoli Faiz Sarraj is considered an Islamist, a proponent of the introduction of Sharia norms in the country.
To what extent does he have a radical opinion?
Wouldn’t that become an obstacle in building relations with Russia or the West?
I'll tell you my personal opinion about him.
In my opinion, he, on the other hand, is an opponent of radical Islam.
But the Islamists are in its coalition.
Yes, but himself adheres to the position that Livia should be an absolutely normal country - a temperately Islamic, open to peace.
And he also actively fights against terrorists.
So where does he get such a reputation?
It was created by those countries that are not interested in Russia communicating with Tripoli.
Tripoli - this is the capital, there is the legislative, executive and judicial authorities.
There is a national oil corporation, the national bank and other state structures.
Of course, some countries were interested that we did not climb there.
And we mixed all the cards to them and began to actively communicate with Tripoli and Tobruk.
Rosneft signed an agreement on a cooperation agreement with the state oil company of Libya - NOC.
NOC Director Mustafa Sanalla, with whom Rosneft CEO Igor Sechin concluded a deal, himself directly from Tripoli.
And two weeks ago there was the first shipment of Libyan oil to Rosneft.
What is Russia going to do about it?
I'm guessing reselling.
And what are Russia's economic interests in Libya?
In plans to rewrote the contracts concluded under Muammar Gaddafi.
We are talking, in particular, about the previous agreements in the transport sector (construction of railways), energy (electrification) and a number of others.
Do Libyan people have anything to pay?
They've got oil.
That is, we are talking, as in the case of Iran, we are talking about an “oil in exchange for services”?
I don't know what the diagram will be, I don't directly deal with these issues.
In fact, the economy for Russia in Libya is not the most important thing.
In fact, we are engaged in peacekeeping work there.
For us, the main thing is to stop the bloodshed, to help the Libyans to negotiate among themselves, so that they can establish an order at home and Libya has ceased to be a favorable environment for the development of terrorism.
For Russia, this main task is to help the Libyan people and squeeze terrorists out.
Do you have information about the presence of radical militants from Russia or other countries of the former USSR in Libya (now or earlier or earlier?
One of the tasks of our contact group was to find out this.
I was meeting with a representative of the Libyan State Security Committee, who said that to this day there is not a single person from Russia and other countries of the former USSR.
He said that he has about 50 thousand entries of telephone calls from representatives of Islamist and Radical groups (in Libya - "Kommersant") and the Russian speech does not sound there.
And from what states are these militants?
I wouldn’t want to go into these details.
Let's formulate a question differently.
How many among Islamist militants in Libya are the Libyans themselves?
There are practically no Libyans among them, they are not more than 5%.
The others are strangers.
Can Moscow hold an intra-Libyan talks on the example of Paris?
There are such plans.
We conduct active negotiations with the Libyans, several delegations from Libya have already visited Moscow, and expressed their readiness to come - Moscow or Grozny.
And when can such negotiations take place?
It’s hard to say right now.
Several more visits should take place, and then, I hope, there will be clarity about the time and place of the negotiations.
In the Chekhov Museum benefactors collected the money on an expensive gift to a sick boy
In the suburban museum-reserve "Melikhovo" a nine-year-old boy Sasha Matsola, whose cerebral cerebral cerebral cotta and complete blossom, on August 5 will receive a specialized treadmill.
Useful presentation will be presented to Sasha by the Minister of culture of the Moscow region Oksana Kosareva and the museum director Konstantin Bobkov.
