Mischel Carter's Sentence for Messages Prompting Conrad Roy
The resident of Massachusetts was sentenced to two and a half years in prison for the fact that with the help of text messages and phone calls to the suicide of her boyfriend Konrad Roy.
Mischel Carter, who is now 20 years old, will have to serve 15 months of his term behind bars and another 5 years of probation.
In June, Carter was found guilty of the minor murder of Conrad Roy, who committed suicide on July 13, 2014.
Roy’s father said at Thursday’s hearing: “My family is gratappled by grief.
"My son was my best friend."
Carter was allowed to remain at large until an appeal.
She was faced with a maximum sentence of 20 years, but her lawyers said that both she and Roy were suffering from mental disorders.
Carter, dressed in red trousers and a creed blouse, listened to the verdict standing, squeezing her hands and lowering her eyes.
“With her actions she killed Konrad Roy”, – said the prosecutor.
“She interrupted his life in order to improve her.
“She didn’t plead guilty,” she said.
“She didn’t show remorse.”
Carter's lawyer said that it was a "tragorical case that she is deeply sorry about."
Judge Lawrence Monis said, in his opinion, her “increducibility, puberty level or even mental illness hasn’t had a pronounce noticeable effect.”
The prosecutor retook the statements of Roy Lynn Roy, which states: “It hasn’t passed a single day when I wouldn’t mourn the loss of my beloved son.
I want him to be proud of me and the way I can handle - I try to support his sisters, in spite of all the pain that will remain with us forever," he said.
The Sister of the Roya Kamdin Roy said that her responsiveness is haunted that she will never be able to be present at his wedding or become his children's aunt.
Choosing a man who has always been with me since my birth is the pain that will stay with me for the rest of my life,” she said.
This case seems to become a legal precedent, since there is no law in Massachusetts, which would provide for responsibility for counseling to commit suicide.
In 2014, when Roye was found in the car dead with symptoms of carbon monoxide poisoning, Carter was 17 years old.
The incident attracted the attention of the whole country, when it became known that he was pushed to the suicidal episcop of Carter.
“If you can hang, jump from the roof, stab you don’t know a lot of ways,” she wrote in several messages sent two weeks before his death, when he was vacationing with his family.
A few minutes before the suicide, she wrote: "You have to do this, Konrad" and "You only need to turn on the ignition, and you will become free and happy."
Judge Monys said Carter wanted to gain attention through Roy’s death and forbade her to communicate with the press so he wouldn’t let her get what she wanted.
Judgments have been divided on this.
One of the few who defended Carter was Amanda Knox, who was sentenced in 2007 for the murder of her British apartmentmate in Italy and acquitted it two years.
30-year-old Knox published in the “Los Angeles Times” her dissimilar opinion, which stated: “Michel Carter deserves sympathy and help, not prison”.
