“Audi” will have to modify up to 850 000 diesel cars
The other day before the announcement from the “Audi” “BMW” stated that it will be proposed to update the software in more than 350 000 cars.
The BMW chairman said that the company believes that "there are more intelligent pathways than driving restrictions", referring to European cities - including Munich, where BMW is located - which considered the ability to prohibit or limit the use of diesel cars.
“Daimler” said on Thursday it will modify three million Mercedes cars in Europe to reduce their diesel exhaust.
None of the companies called their move a review.
European automakers actively promoted the use of diesel cars in Europe and the United States in order to contribute to compliance with carbon dioxide emitation rules.
But nitric oxides that emit diesel engines are considered carcinogenic and can cause asphthma.
The cost for automakers to install equipment that neutralizes the exhaust gases of diesel cars also rises, and it is becoming difficult to maintain a competitive price for cars.
While German automakers are under scrutiny attention, Chancellor Angela Angela Merkel’s government was also accused of indulging influential automakers and ignoring signs of a problem.
Companies try not to replicate the errors of “Volkswagen”, which hid the use of so-called “defeat devices”, which during testing could tweak the amount of harmful gases emitted so that it complied with the rules, and in the conditions of normal driving turned off.
In the United United States was convicted by several leaders of “Volkswagen”, the rest are under investigation on both sides of the Atlantic.
Last month in Germany arrested the former head of the thermodynamics department as part of the Audi engine development group.
Former manager, Zackeo Giovanni Pamío, an Italian, and therefore is not protected from extradition and can stand trial in the United States.
Earlier this year, “Audi” came under the German criminal investigation involving “Volkswagen” after the authorities accused “Audi” of installing a system to bypass European emit rules and expanded the investigation, which was previously focused on the United States.
Incorporating “Audi” in the investigation can create a serious problem “Volkswagen”: a manufacturer of luxury cars is a source of disproportionately a large share of “Volkswagen”.
In Astrakhan, the visitor of the café paid with falsified money
The police received a message from the employee of the branch of the bank about the discovery when recalculating the funds of funds received from the point of catering, a suspicious bill in denominated in denomination of 5 thousand rubles.
A study carried out at the Forensitological Center showed that it is false.
According to the Ministry of internal Affairs of Russia in the Astrakhan region, one of the visitors of the café, who bought shawarma, paid the banknote.
It is worth noting that the cash register was not equipped with a device for determining the autibility of banknotes.
At the present time, the police are establishing persons involved in the manufacture and sale of a deliberately counterfeit ticket of the Central Bank of the Russian Federation.
Such crimes are punished by imprisonment for up to 8 years with a fine in the amount of up to 1 million rubles.
The regional Department of the Ministry of internal Affairs urges residents of the Astrakhan region to be attentive when performing financial transactions; employees of trade objects are recommended to install devices to verify the authenticity of the funds received.
Astronomers have found an “hellish” planet on which even iron can melt
For the first time after studying the properties of the stratospheres of a giant exoplanet called WASP-121b, astrophysicists were quite amazed by its temperature, which is able to veliberate iron and other metals.
Specialists drew attention to the fact that the water molecules are so heated with the light of the star that infrared is emitted.
Telescope "Hubble" captured the glorification of water molecules on this gas giant: this high temperature causes water to glow in the planet's infrared.
WASP-121b belongs to the so-called "hot Jupiters" - gas giants, in terms of size and weight comparable to the largest planet of the solar system, but located ten times closer to the parent star.
Because of this year on the exoplanet lasts only 1.3 “terrestrial” days”, and its gas envelope is heated to almost 2 500 degrees Celsius.
Climate change is ignoring lavender in Provence.
She has become a symbol of Provence and southern France, but now there are fears that it is threatened by climate change.
Lavender began to grow worse due to arid weather and insidious insect diseases; this was the cause of a constant headache for scientists and farmers who are trying to find a solution.
Eric Sches, an expert at Provence, an expert at the CRIEPPAM Agricultural Research Institute, said: “Lavenda in Provence is indeed at risk because in recent years this plant has felt the consequences of climate change: in the spring and especially autumn, the rain has become much smaller.
This Affects lavender’s lifespan.
And there are still small cicadas, jumping on the leaves insect, carrying micro-bacteriums; in very dried-cash weather they become a very large.
Attached a lot is at stake.
Lavender not only attracts vacationers; lavender oil is very popular in perfumery and cosmetology.
Eric Shees says: "Instead of very long ears with a large number of large colors, we have small, underdeveloped, impregnable, or even missing.
Therefore, we have fewer parts containing essential butter.”
Solutions that are currently under consideration include improving the distribution of the water and decelerating evaporation from the soil, as well as sprinkling plants with a protective mixture of clay and water and extinguishing varieties more resistant to drought.
