Creating a Réry Comic: A Castle in English Stories
In the recent past, Skotney's tiny castle was filmed in the musical video "Squeeze", and in the 70's and 80's it served as a haven for Margaret Thatcher.
But for 700 years from his cozy place in the valley of the Beul River, he observed a turbulent history around, and now inspired Jamie Rhodes, Yorkshire with copied hair and penchant for historical documents, on a comedian.
"It seems to me that it's so beautiful - to look to the handwriting of the man who died 300 years ago," he says with excitement.
"You feel it so personally when you keep this letter in your hand."
“Class in England” covers the period from Medium-sized centuries to the Evidrian era and talks about families who lived in Scotny; every story was illustrated by one of the young British artists – Isaac Lenkevich, Bryoni May Smith, William Exley, Becky Palmer and Isabel Grinberg.
This isn’t Rod’s first book based on archifious data: in 2014, he wrote “The Teeth of a Dead Man and Other Stories”, a collection of documents from the British LibéfurcATION; this project unexpectedly touched it to the deepest.
“I could just touch the fingerprint on the edge of the letter, written in the 1700-ies by a double agent who worked for Jacobites,” he says.
"It's his fingerprint"
And the letters always smell of smoke, because in those days a fire was ignited to illuminate.
And after 300 years, in the future, it seems to you that you are also there.
Oh, how much I love the archives!"
For a man grased with such a passion for old papers to gain support from the National Focal Foundation and the British Art Council and to live in the castle for four months (“Honstantially, I’m a little settled there”) seems too good to be the truth.
Rhodes throughout the day studied the "new" Victorian castle, walked through the archives and looked at numerous treasures of the estate and antiquities - for example, hyena's heads on the walls or bottles that have been lying in the motter for centuries.
He walked in the park and on the ruins of the old castle, talked with foresters, gardeners and sometimes with artists who worked on the illustrations for his book.
Then at night he drank whiskey and slept to peat.
Scotney's castle history is not very well studied because the National Foodeship gained full access to it only in 2006 when the last heiress, Elizabeth Hassey, died.
When Rhodes arrived there in ten years, employees were just beginning to deal with the archive, which he describes as “that the aristocrats for centuries have blamed for an attic.”
Diaries, letters from the times of the British Empire, maps showing who owned what: "You think land disputes are boring," says Rods, "but this birch two families were beating for this birch.
It's like that, guys!"
In some of the stories of the collection, the castle becomes the starting point for wider research in English history: for example, in the "Emergency", the hero goes away from the newly built castle to join the Peasant revolution of 1381.
“There is information about the riot, which took place in the castle in 1380, in a book titled “Cimmersiastic Families of Kent and Sussex,” says Rhodes.
“Perprising revolt began in these places, and I thought the riot was a good start.
“Maybe they’re connected?”
Other stories are firmly connected with the history of the castle - for example, "The Priest", which talks about the Jesuit Priest, whom the Darrelov family hid for seven years during the British Reformation.
“Smuggler”, about an 18th-century smuggler, Arthur Darrell, who is believed to have staged his own vocabulary with a coffin (this was discovered a few-thought a few-thought after the coffin was culpted).
Darrells - Rhodes's favorite family of everything that was inhabited by Cattle: "Gentlemen, it seems to have been a perfect scam, forever got into debt and spent money on something they couldn't afford.
In different generations, Darrela men solved their problems with their debates, marrying rich elderly women - I see them as a company of pretty guys who are able to care for the heiaries of great states.
After graduating, Rhodes is looking for other opportunities to gain a unique writer’s experience.
He lived for two weeks in the Finnish wilderness, where he wrote a graphic novel about Elamyanmäki - the place where at the beginning of the 20th century there was a sanatorium, and then overgrown with a timber again overgrown with forest.
Scotny remains a special place for him.
“I was sad to leave,” he said.
“I’ve felt something like this: the hell, I have to go back to real life again.”
Fifteen of the largest banks choose “Romania”
The conflict in the Association of Russian banks is developing: after Sberbank, VTB, VTB-24, Alfa-bank, Gazprombank, Rosselkhozbank, Binbank and FC Otkritie, seven other credit institutions are going to leave this public organization.
Thus, the share of organizations released out of ARB will account for at least 80 percent of the market.
But this is not just a way out - all the banks that announced the breakaway ARB, are negotiating with another public organization, uniting credit institutions - the Association of regional banks "Rossiya", headed by a well-known politician Anatoly Aksakov, the Chairman of the State Duma Committee on the financial market, recognized, by the result of the last session and the most effective head of the Duma committee and the deputy in the number of prepared bills.
The beginning of the conflict within ARB was established during the discussion in the Federation Council, when the Interregional Banking Council considered new bills, in particular, involving a new classification of banks, depending on the size of the authorized capital.
Then Garegin Tosunyang, the President of ARB, said that, in the opinion of the association, this bill is adopted in the interests of the largest banks, which are thus trying to limit the capabilities of small and medium-sized banks in the regions, intercepting their customers.
Among the other claims there was also a critique against the Central Bank, who, according to Tosunyana, does not always justifiably carry out the revocation of licenses from some of the banks, which, however, there was an objection from the representative of the Central Bank: many heads of penitentiary banks, in particular, Vneshprombank, were included in the governing bodies of ARB.
Apparently, this exchange of mutually-exclusivating opinions in a very sensitive relationship with the main regulator of the banking environment and became an obvious reason for the fifteen largest banks, declaring their disagreement with ARB’s policy, begin to prepare for joining the association “Russia”, noting that “the effectiveness of ARBS is at a low level, and a constructive dialogue within the banking community is actually not carried out.”
Contributors will be better
How's it gonna end?
We will immediately answer the main question, which arises at the slightest failure or a conflict in the banking sector or next to it: depositors do not face anything, rather, on the contrary, the reliability of the banking system will increase.
Anatoly Aksakov is headed by “Russia”, known for his scrupulousness in everything that concerns the interests of banks and their customers, a high-level professional who is highly valued in the Central Bank: almost the entire management of the Central Bank is present at the annual activities of the association, and all significant legislative initiatives of the regulator pass through expert assessments of “regionals”.
In the calibration-organizational plan, obviously, there are also no special upheavals.
Undoubtedly, ARB falls into an uneasable financial and managerial situation after losing such powerful and influential participants with their contributions and lobbying opportunities.
However, there are considerable potential in this, the institution that defends the interests of the banking community in 1991 in order to continue to improve banking and monetary circulation as a whole in order to continue to improve banking and monetary circulation as a whole.
It is impossible to say that the association "Rosiya" is ready to accept on any conditions of new members, judging by the reaction of its leader, Anatoly Aksakov ("maybe too much want"), who on July 21 at a briefing in the press center of the Parliamentary Newspaper, said that "literally the next day, the representatives of banks who came out of ARB have asked me to consider the possibility of increasing the capacity of our Rossi Association."
Their proposals - to amplify the votes of bankers in the Association's Council, as well as to pay more attention to new banking technologies.
Now the negotiation process is underway, proposals of both sides are being explored, an agenda is being prepared for an extraordinary congress of the association, which will be held in Sochi in mid-September as part of an international banking forum.
That's what we'll decide.
Anatoly Aksakov, emphasizing, stressing that "doesn't hold for a chair", called Georgy Luntovsky, a possible new head of the updated association "Rossiya", who released the post of deputy chairman of the Central Bank in September, highly characterizing its business and human qualities.
On August 18, Anatoly Aksakov, who is currently resting in the Crimea, plans to interrupt his vacation and come to Moscow for an extraordinary meeting of the Rossiya Association’s Council, where it is planned to consider the agenda of an extraordinary congress “Rosiya”.
