“As part of the investigation of the criminal case initiated under Art. 116 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation (“Beatings”) against a 32-year-old man who punched a correspondent of one of the TV channels in the Gorky Central Park and Recreation, the suspect was chosen a preventive measure in the form of a recognizance of not leaving and proper behavior,” Volk said.
The representative of the Ministry of internal Affairs added that an administrative protocol has been drawn up for disobedience to the police against the suspect.
On Wednesday, August 2, during a live broadcast to the Airborne People’s Airborne People’s Airborne Day, a drunk man approached the correspondent and punched in the face.
As it turned out later, the hooligan has nothing to do with VDV.
According to Razvozzhaev himself, the paratroopers, on the contrary, tried to detain a Muscovite.
