The U.S. foreign Ministry accused the Vice-President of the U.S. in rhetoric during the cold war
Claims, made during the European tour of Vice-President of the United States Michael Pence, were criticized by the Russian foreign Ministry.
“It is regrettable to state that Washington is increasingly sliding into the primitive ideculated tranqushes of the Cold War”, which are completely detached from reality,” the Russian foreign ministry said in a statement.
So the foreign Ministry reacted to the words of Pence about the “Russian threat” and attempts to forcibly redrawing the borders said by him in Podgorica.
The Russian foreign Ministry pointed to the destructiveness of the choice "either with the West, or with Russia" and the non-obedience to the thesis about the allegedly uncontributory entry of the entire South-Eastern Europe into NATO.
Russian diplomats also reminisced that the United States violated international law, applying force to dismantle Kozov from Serbia and thus created another source of tension.
“We call on American colleagues to stop languishing Russia and its foreign policy, which invariably is based on respect for its partners and readiness for joint constructive work on a mutual consideration of their interests”, – said in a statement of the Russian foreign Ministry.
