And already in August you have planned a concert in Monaco, not ordered, but a poster, right?
Yes, in Monte-Carlo there is a good "Sporting room", I've already performed there one day.
Now invited again, and, as far as I know, all the tickets for the concert have already been sold out.
On "Rendeeva Laima Vaikule", which will begin on July 20 in Jurmala, are you going?
She invited me, and of course I responded.
Laima is a wonderful singer and a gorgeous woman who knows how to present herself and beautiful vocals, and even a whisper.
After the touring and anniversary celebrations, as far as I know, you once again want to turn to Vladimir Vysotsky.
You already have two albums with his songs in your discography.
When's the third one coming out?
Possibly next year.
But it will be done in a completely different way.
I want to record about 80-90 Vysotsky's songs about the same serve as he did himself.
Only a voice and a Guitar.
There's no other arrangement.
I will be accompanied by our well-known musician Timur Vedernikov.
I will try to attract Alexander Yakovlevich Rosenbaum to participate in the album.
I talked this topic with him, we have a good relationship, but he is a busy person, so let's see what will turn out.
You and Boris Grebenshchikov's songs gradually entered into your repertoire.
Maybe you're gonna put up the album of his stuff later?
Boris Borisovich is a wonderful person and a great musician.
I intersected with him several times and asked: can I sing this or another of his songs?
"Gregory, I'm singing songs so they're singing."
Please try it, sing.
It’s also interesting to record such an album.
While I don’t have such a task yet, but in the future, in a year-two, if Boris Boris Borisovich doesn’t bother, I’ll probably make such a project.
If you don’t fully focus on the affairs of your production center.
Suppose you haven’t already realized its potential, I haven’t signed contracts with all the artists that you’re interested in?
There are a number of performers whom I would dream of having under my porridge, but they are an independent, accommodating people.
Do you mean Sergey Lazarev?
Serezha is a shiny singer, I invited him.
I don’t want to disagree with his repertoire, but he is a professional and he has his own development strategy.
And in my center now there is Alexander Panariotov, whom I led in the "Voice".
We signed a contract with him and we are working.
In our pop music, such singers are unparalleled.
It will be a pity if it does not reach the elevations that he is worthy.
I'm trying to pick up his repertoire, I'm filming clips.
I'm looking forward to a good result.
Also, I try to promote other artists of my center: I buy them songs, I cry to the poets, sometimes their tracks fall into the rotations of television and radio channels.
If they don't reach great heights, I'll still bring our cooperation to a logical conclusion.
At the output they will receive a recorded album, a few clips.
And then, if they wish, they can go their own way, and I won't insist that they return the money invested in them.
Although I will be pleased if one of them achieves commercial succulitis and will pay me the interest that we negotiated in the contract.
But if this does not happen, I'm not going to cover the oxygen to anyone.
Let them all work, break through, prove how I once proved.
If tomorrow you will be offered a touring tour of Ukraine and guarantee entry to the country, will you go?
I'm still being invited.
It’s mostly about closed events.
As for the big tour...
I am a person of my country, a Russian, by his own opinion, flew to Syria on the same plane, which then crashed.
If tomorrow they say that you need to fly to some other point in the interests of the state - I will fly.
I don’t care what bloggers and other critics are going to think about me.
I sincerely deplore that such a situation turned out to be with Ukraine.
Since I think: we are one people and we should be together.
I’m sorry I don’t think this will work, at least in the near future.
And I used to give 40-50 concerts in a year in Ukraine every year.
Met, like nowhere.
It's a very grateful audience.
And with several Ukrainian artists cooperated: Ani Lorak, Sveta Loboda, Artyom Loik...
In Ukraine there are a lot of gifted people, and it is a pity that now they can not fully throw out their talent to a broad Russian audience.
Music should unite and amplify people.
I'd be happy to invite some great Ukrainian performer to Russia, such as Glory Vakarchuk, and made a concert together with him.
I don't think at the moment it's unprepared...
Andrey Okhlopkov was transferred from the cosmodrome
As it became known to "Kommersant", the technical director of the Vostochny Cosmodrome Andrey Okhlopkov began to work in the Khrunichev State Space Research and Production Center.
Earlier, he was de facto engaged in the construction of the Vostochny cosmodrome, but due to disagreements with the management of the Center for the operation of terrestrial and space infrastructure (TSENKI) was transferred to the enterprise in the Moscow Fili, where he will coordinate the production.
There will be no changer from Okloptskov: the post of technical director will most likely be abolished, and the functionality is scattered according to TsENKI units.
The fact that the technical director of Vostochny's Eastern and the deputy general's General Director for Technological Development Andrey Okhlopkov switched to work at Khrunichev's SCNPC, Kommersant was told by top managers of several enterprises of the space industry, as well as an employee of the government apparatus.
“He has been working in a new post for several weeks”, – said the interlocutors of “Kommersant” in the industry.
IT was not Possible to receive an operative comment from TsENKI on Thursday, and Mr. Okhlopkov himself was unavailable for comments.
However, Kommersant information was officially officially confirmed by SCNPC.
He made a decision on the transition to the position of director for the coordination of production, - said at the enterprise. - Andrey Okhlytkov assigned to him the task of ensuring the starting minimum for the first launch at the Vostochny cosmodrome has fully complieded.
Mr. Okhlopkov moved to work in TSENKI in 2013, having service in the space army, in particular on Baikonur, and in Plesetsk - at the "northern" cosmodrome held the post of first deputy commander in the rank of colonel.
In 2009, Andrey Okhloptkov became a defendant in a criminal case.
The investigation blamed him for bribe-and-employment: allegedly with its filing, regional merchants received state-supplies, but did not fulfill their obligations to clean separated parts of carrier rockets in the Arkhangelsk region and the Komi Republic.
In 2012, a jury pleaded not guilty.
responsibilities for technological development entrusted to him in TSENKI were extended to various projects, but most of them was the construction of a cosmodrome in the Far East.
Oleg Ostapenko, who then headed the Federal Space Agency in an “Kommersant” bluntly said that the state of affairs on Vostochny “were critical in October 2013”.
The fact is that a strategic mistake was made during the planning: the completion of the construction and the first launch of the Soyuz-2.1 carrier rocket were planned at the same time - at the end of 2015.
In order to launch by the end of the second of the year, it was decided to complete the construction for six months earlier and the terms were shifted from December to July 2015.
To accelerate the process, it was necessary to make a cunnaded trick: TSENKI specialists began to conduct a parallel installation of technological equipment at unfinished facilities.
The main proponent of this idea was Andrey Oloptkov.
In spite of the existing risks and still the transfer that happened (instead of December 2015, “Soyuz” left only on April 28, 2016), this idea accumulators acquitted itself, a Kommersant source says at the cosmodrome: “We would still not carry out a single launch from Vostochny, but were engaged in construction.”
Deputy Prime Minister Dmitry Rogozin, who oversees the creation of the cosmodrome, jokingly called Andrey Okhlopkov his “cosmic Susanin”, but he almost always requested information about the course of the construction.
I am remembered Mr. Olopkhtkov and straightforward: for example, in an interview with Kommersant, he proposed to deprive the Federal Agency for special construction (Spetsstroy) as the only performer in the East and directly work with sub-contractors: "Why do we have to lay all the eggs in the same basket of Spetsstroy?"
This idea found support in the government.
Since 2017, TSENKI has assumed the responsibilities of the general contractor in order to complete construction and installation work on the starting and technical complex scheduled in the fourth Quarter.
According to Kommersant, the reason for the transition of Mr. Oloptshkov to a new place of work was the disagreements with the management of TSENKI regarding the ways to complete the construction of structures and complexes of the cosmodrome, as well as methods of working with subcontracting organizations.
“It was agreed that this would be better for everyone,” says one of the top managers participating in the construction of Vostochny.
An employee of the government apparatus, in turn, calls the solution strange: "He was one of the best specialists, it will not be easy to find an equivalent replacement for him."
According to "Kommersant", this will not be necessary: the position of technical director of the cosmodrome will be abolished, and its functions will be scattered to the units of TsENKI.
In musical schools there will be a program of training for two specialties
In the future, pupils of children's music schools will be able to receive two specialties at the same time.
Svyatoslav Golubenko, deputy director of the department of science and education of the Ministry of Culture, you can re-enter the students of repeated disciplines, and the issue with the payment of other classes in the second specialty is solved with the help of special grants, RIA Novosti reports.
“The Ministry of culture took this issue under control, and we, together with the expert community, will develop a mechanism that will allow us to develop two specialties, but at the same time will not contradict the current legislation in the field of education,” Golubenko said.
Last Friday, a student Maria Andreeva said that she was forced to pay for repetitive tracerebral subjects with pupils of the Sirius children's center "Syrius" that she was forced to pay for recurring items for the second specialty at the CMSU at the Moscow Conservatory.
The girl said that she is studying in violin and piano class and has awards of competitions in both directions.
The head of state recognized her issue very topical and promised to help.
In Mexico detained 17-year-old Russian climbed on the wall on a skyscraper
In Mexico detained 17-year-old Russian Kirill N., who climbed the wall on the roof of a high-altitude building, according to the portal El Universal.
