Users called the young man a “spider-Man”.
According to media reports, such experiments are a hobby for him.
Red meawargs, dairy products, and chocolate can help relieve IBD.
Celestial meat and chocolate are considered a nightmare for your digestive tidy trunk.
But recent research suggests the opposite: a diet rich in berries and mammacies can help relieve symptoms in those suffering from inflammatory bowel disease.
This is an incurable disease, which affects approximately 1.3 million people in the U.S. and $300000 in the U.K. lead to colic and bloating, chronic or blood diarrhea, weight loss and extreme fatigue.
Typically to soften symptoms, the patients are advised to avoid meat and dairy products, but researchers from the U.N. at the University of Washington found that the main amino acid tryptophan protein contributes to the production of immune cells that increase gut tolerance.
The leading researcher Dr. Marco Colonna explained that immune cells in the intestinium make sure that harmful microbes coming from food do not enter the body.
Cells, which are able to start an inflammatory process, are balancing cells that increase tolerability, protecting the body without detriment of sensitive thuns.
If the equilibrium is too much imperfringed towards inflammation, this can lead to inflammatory bowel diseases.
experiments have shown that in mice with a certain bacterium in the intestinium, there is an increasing tolerance of cells.
And this bacterium needs tryptophan - one of the building elements of the protein - to start the appearance of these cells.
Professor Colonna said: "We have established a link between a single type of bacteria - Lactobacillus reuteri - which is part of the normal gut microbiome, and the development of a population of cells that increase tolerance.
The more tryptophan was contained in the nutrition of the mice, the more these immune cages they had.”
He speculated that the same thing would work in people: a combination of L. reuteri and tryptophan-rich diet may contribute to a more tolerant and less pronounced specimen in the intestinium.
Posstock Dr. Luisa Cervantes-Barraganabas, studying a type of immune cell-enclosing tolerance, found that one group of guinea pigs had these cells, and the other group, which belonged to the same line, but contained separately, they didn't have them.
She hypothesized that the difference could be caused by intestinal germ burial mushrooms - communities of bacteria, viruses and fungi, which usually live in the gastrointestinal tract.
The DNA of intestinal cells of the intestinium of the mice was sequenced, and six species of bacteria were detected in mice that have immune cells but are absent in mice that do not have them.
Muses grown in a sterile militarium that didn’t have a good microbiome and did not develop this type of immune cells received L. reuteri and their immune cages appeared.
In order to understand how the bacteriums affect the immune system, the researchers grew L. reuteri in a liquid environment and then transferred small portions of fluid - without bacteria - to underdeveloped immune cells isolated from the mice.
Immune cells have turned into cells that increase tolerability.
When the active component was disgusted from the liquor, it turned out to be a byproduct of tryptophan, known as indole-3 lactic acid.
When the researchers dodged tryptophan in the meal of mice, the number of these cells increased by about 50 per cent, but when tryptophan levels were halved, the number of cells also halved.
Doctor Cervantes-Barragán explains that people have the same tolerant-producing ciliaries as in mice, and most of us have L. reuteri in their gastrointestinal tract.
It is not known whether tryptophan spicy products from L. reuteri the development of cells in humans, as well as in mice, but people who suffer from inflammatory bowel diseases have been found to have defects in triptophan genes.
She says: "Perhapposes the development of these cells should be strengthened, since inflammatory processes on the inner intestinium depends on these cells.
“High levels of tryptophan if L. reuteri can potentially lead to an enlargement of their population.”
According to Jose Mourinho, “Manchester United” hired a “genius” in the person of Nemanja Matic
“Manchester United” hired a “genius” represented by Nemanya Matic, believes Jose Mourinho after the midfielder made his debut against Sampdoria on Wednesday evening.
The player, acquired for £40 million from Chelsea, began with a score of 2-1 in Dublin in the last pre-season match of “United” ahead of the UEFA Super Cup match against “Real Madrid” on Thursday and made an imitation in the role of a midfielder, while players like Paul Pogba and Andreas Pereira broke through when they wanted.
Nevertheless, since Matic did not take part in Chelsea pre-season in Asia, he seriously lacked preparations for the game, and he withstood only 45 minutes, which, according to Mourinho, requires refinement before the start of the Premier League season.
“He needs a time, but his experience, his mind, a genius, a genius in the way he thinks – he thinks football,” Mourinho said.
“We’re going to help him prepare sooner rather than it’s too late.”
Just, like Matich, his comrades-new players, Victor Lindelöf and Romelu Lukaku began a game at Aviv Stadium when Mourinho began shaping its main line-up at the beginning of next season.
“Indignant Newspaper” reported this week that Mourinho wanted to hire three more players, but emphasized that the club has already achieved fantastic results, hiring three of the four players that he would like to hire in the first place.
“I am grateful to the club for having produced three out of four,” he said.
“I’d rejoice even more if they get me four out of four, but they’ve already done a great job for me.”
The former Lithuanian Social-Democrat Leader Congratulations Rejoiced at Staying in Ruling Coalition
The former chairmen of the Social Democratic Party of Lithuania, ex-premiers Algirdas Butkevičius and Gediminas Kirkilas, as well as the former Sejm of the Sejm from Social-Democrats Cheslovas Jurchenas, appealed to fellow party members with an enema to remain in the ruling coalition.
As reported "Parliamentary Gazette", because of friction with its partners - the Union of Peasants and "Greens" in the Social-Democratic party initiated a discussion about whether it is necessary to remain in the ruling coalition.
And here are the three senior experienced comrades appealed to fellow party members with an open letter, in which, in particular, it is said: “It is understandable to the disappointment of comrades on the party the results of the elections, but the coalition with “Preprismen” has created, albeit not very easily for us, but still the conditions for the further implementation of social justice goals, which, on our initiative, are provided for in the program of the government and to preserve the political dominion of the left center over right-wing parties.”
According to the former leaders of the party, in the discussion so for the so far “experience-based expression of opinion without specific arguments”, prevailed.
The authors of the letter are wary of ignorant actions of their party can lead Lithuania to political, economic and social instability.
Disability Anton Mamaev imposed a fine
The Moscow city court commensured the punishment of a visually impatient wizard Anton Mamayev from four and a half years of imprisonment to a fine of 200 thousand rubles.
Earlier, the decision of the Timiryazevsky court, the convict was released from the pre-trial detention center.
At the same time, the Moscow city court confirmed that the accused is a criminal, since he organized the robber and the abduction of a scooter from a former special forces soldier.
The Moscow city court by his decision mitigated the punishment of Anton Mamaev to 200 thousand rubles. fine.
“Mamaev is the organizer of the robbery, which also forms a crime, and, accordingly, such a person should be brought to criminal responsibility,” Ulyana Solopova, a press secretary of the Moscow City Court, told Kommersant.
In this case the court took into account Mamayev's state of health, the actual circumstances of the case, the absence of aggravating circumstances.
In addition, the court applied Art. 64 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation, according to which it is possible to impose a punishment below the lower limit.
As for Mamayev's assistant Vasily Seroshtanov, the court did not establish the circumstances that would become the basis for changes in the category of gravity of the act and changing the verdict.
Anton Mamaev himself said that he remained dissatisfied with the decision of the Moscow City Court.
Disappointed by a court decision.
The only lawful solution would be an acquiescence, it intends to continue to fight for justice.
His lawyer Andrey Orlov did not preclude an appeal of the verifiment in the cassation instance of the Moscow City Court and the Verkhovna court.
“We will use all leeches up to the European court of human rights”, – he told RIA Novosti.
We will remind, the 28-year-old Muscovite Anton Mamaev, suffering from spinal muscular atrophy, became a defendant in the criminal case in the fall of last year.
Disableda claims that he bought a scooter from friends for 160 thousand rubles, in order to then sell.
However, the owners of the scooter, among whom - a former special forces fighter, said that the disabled and his assistant Vasily Seroshtanov took away their property, threatening to use the violence.
On June 30, Timiryazevsky district court of Moscow sentenced Vasily Seroshtanov to three years in a colony, and Anton Mamaev - to four and a half years in prison with serving a sentence in a colony of the general regime (under Part 2 of Art. 162 of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation).
After the immovable invalid was placed in a pre-trial detention facility, Tatiana Moskalkova, Commissioner for human rights under the President Tatyana Moskalkov joined the case.
AS a result, in mid-July, Anton Mamaev was released from the SIZO by a decision of the same Timiryazevsky court.
The defense, in turn, appealed the decision of the first instance in the Moscow city court.
THE ONF will prepare a report to the president on ecology
The final “Forum of actions” of the All-Russian popular front (ONF) in 2017 will be devoted to environmental issues, told “Izvestia” a source in the ONF and confirmed the head of the Executive Committee of the movement Alexei Anisimov.
According to him, according to the results of the forum "Frontline soldiers" plan to prepare a report to the president on the problems of domestic ecology, as well as to propose a strategy for their solution.
Interlocutors of “Izvestia” in the ONF note that the report to the head of the state will contain “deep analysis” on the situation in all federal districts of the country.
According to “Izvestia”, the final ONF forum will take place in the autumn.
the exact date of its holding has not yet been determined - as a rule, it adapts to the schedule of the President, who is the leader of the movement and is traditionally present at the key ONF events.
The front held several inter-regional environmental conferences, one for two federal counties - in Rostov-on-Don, Kaliningrad and Kirov.
The final conference will be held in the capital of the Republic of Buryatia Ulan-Ude.
On the basis of the proposals that were expressed and will be expressed at these events, we will form systemic proposals to solve environmental problems, the interlocutor in the ONF told Izvestia.
The co-chairman of the Central headquarters of the movement Olga Timofeeva, who heads the state Duma Committee on ecology and protection of the environment, said that the “front” will inform the head of the state on the work carried out within the framework of the Year of Ecology in Russia.
The final environmental forum and the ONF Moderum for Action will most likely be reconciled.
For a year we overgrown a powerful team of experts in the field of environmental problems, saw gaps in the legislation, stopped dozens of violations of the law.
All this will be included in the report, which we are preparing to the president as the leader of our movement.
In addition to this document, "Frontmen" will report on the work on the priority projects of the ONF, Olga Timofeeva told Izvestia.
According to her, the special representative of the head of state on issues of environmental activities, ecology and transport Sergey Ivanov will also be invited to the forum.
Previously, he took part in the work of the ONF Mediafum, which was held in St. Petersburg in April.
In a few months the Year of ecology will go into history, and the most important thing you need to do today is to launch environmental mechanisms so that they work for many years.
So that these issues do not fall from the subpoena,” Olga Timofeeva added.
The head of the laboratory of regional policy of the Expert Institute of social studies (EESI), Andrei Kolyadin, noted that raising the environmental problems, the ONF acts in line with the presidential agenda.
Many things they as experts proposed in various forums, and these initiatives received the support of the president,” Andrey Kolyaddin told Izvestia.
He stressed that to this day it is impossible to exclude the economic potential of the ecological agenda, which can give the regions an additional impetus for development.
In the future, with the help of ONF, the regions will be able to lobby not only the solution of their environmental problems, but also the development of ecotourism, the expert added.
Relevance of the environmental themes was demonstrated “secret line” with Vladimir Putin in June.
In particular, the President was questioned about the garbage dump in Balashikha (already closed) and about coal dust in the port of Nakhodka (already a bill has already been developed to prohibit open transshipment of coal in populated areas, one of the authors - Olga Timofeeva).
experts in the field of ecology believe that the legal framework for solving environmental problems in Russia as a whole has been created, the issue lies in the further law enforcement practice, as well as the position of civil society.
It is necessary to clearly implement the decisions taken by the state, ”said Leonid Bochin, head of Ecology for All Charitable Foundation.
Sergei Tsyplenkov in a conversation with “Izvestia” stressed that to successfully solve environmental problems requires a responsible approach of society and business, there is not a lot of legislative efforts to successfully solve environmental problems.
As soon as in society and business they are aware that the solution of environmental problems is a much more favorable step in the strategic perspective, the situation will change,” said Sergey Tsyplenkov.
The expert stressed that it is Necessary to change the tendency to the fact that the infringement of environmental legislation is an economically profitable solution for business.
The British Inventor Imposes a Microchip to Get Into a House and A Car Waving
The British explorer became the first person in the country to install a microchip so that he can open the door of his house, go into the office and even start a car using a simple flapping of his hands.
Thirty-thirteen-year-old Steven Northam implanted a tiny chip between the thumb and an instincile finger, and now, through his company, BioTec offers this service to firms and private individuals who want to simplify their lives at the expense of the technology.
He teamed up with Dr. Jeff Watson, an an anesthesiologist-consultant at the Royal Winchester in Winchester, taking into account that the implantation procedure is carried out in accordance with medical standards.
The technology looks like a microchip, which is implanted in cats and dogs, and the procedure takes only 30 seconds.
Northam is also resettling locks in homes and cars with a chip-compatible for 300 pounds per castle.
Married the father of one of the child has already installed the technology in his car “BMW Z4”, which starts when his hand lies on the steering wheel.
Requisite for the White house cost the taxpayer in a thousand-dolverin
According to military recordings provided to TIME magazine, the White House's decision last month to drive a helicopter of the marine eibling to the Southern lawn for an event dedicated to American industrial production cost taxpayers as much as $ 24 000.
White-Green Sikorsky VH-3D, known as "Marine One", when the board is the president, became a central element held on July 17 at the White House an Event on which U.E. construction programs were shown.
President Donald trump, Vice-President Mike Pence and senior White House officials examined technology products from all fifty states.
Helter, produced in Konnektuk, was exhibited next to a yacht from the state of Main, a fire truck from Wisconsin and fork forklift from the Mississip.
According to the recordings of the First Squadron of Jelle Helicopters (HMX-1), the department responsible for the management of the Helicopter, the White House Warrior ordered the presence of a helm in a private order, or “FRAGO”, just 36 hours before the helicopter landed on the southern lawn on an “unannounced “unannounced” event.
“I just wanted you to make sure that you are aware of, because it’s an unambiguous event widely illuminated in the press,” the HMX-1 commander wrote in an e-white letter to his boss, the first deputy chief of the Marine Corps, on the eve of the event.
In the letter, it was pointed out that the helf will arrive on the Southern lawn at about 7 a.m. on July 17 to participate in an event scheduled for 3 o'clock in the afternoon, and will stay there before the lawn will be vacated between 6 and 9 p.m. on the same day.
In the letter, it is added that if the departure from the White house is delayed, a second crew will be required for a return flight in accordance with restrictions on working hours.
The first crew escorted the helpodilk during the event, and the security of the unit stayed next to the aircraft while it was located on the ground.
From the entries obtained by TIME magazine, it remained unclear whether the second crew was eventually required.
Hitcha law forbids federal employees to use state property for political purposes.
According to entries, HMX-1 specified whether the event is contrary to this resolution.
“At among other things, we’ve been asked whether it’s a violation of Hatch law and we’ve been told it wasn’t,” the commander wrote.
“It doesn’t matter if you don’t have anything to go,” the deputy boss said.
“Made in the United States event” was announced by the White House as an official Event, and Hatch law was not covered.
But even the official events have political notes.
During the course of the event, the President made an Effort to Promote a Healthcare Reform at that time and praised attempts to regulate governmental regulations.
The use of aircraft, known "Marine One" and "Air Force One" for political purposes - hardly a new phenomenon.
Presidents are instructed to use them for travel.
Receiving them is unusual in the interests of photography.
“Trump has already become a matter of discussion in February when the presidential plane rode in the background during his first election rally in Melbourne, in the state of Florida, and his Twitter account was flooded with messages with complaints about the use of the presidential plane by his predecessor.
“White house is enthusiastic about the ‘Made-in-Amerdenous in the Americas, which featured products from 50 states made by U.S. workers from U.S. material,” White House spokeswoman Lindsay Walters said.
HMX-1 crews often conduct training flights around the Washington agglomeranence and on the South Lawn to practice the transportation of the President of the United States to the White House with an inch.
When trump in early July was at the G-20 summit in Germany, HMX-1 conducted 58 training landings near the White House.
According to one of the officials, the float performed for the “Made in the United States”, was numbered to the crew on the result of the necessary training flights for a month.
Helicopters of the unit on that day also raided 11 additional hours as part of “non-presidential support tasks”.
According to the White House, there were no expenses for any of the other exhibits presented at the event.
A spokesman for Sikorsky said that the company did not take part in organizing a demonstration of a helmet on the South lawn.
HMX-1 does not take into account the budget for presidential flights, and it is divulant to determine the exact amount expended for the event.
But, according to Department of Defense’s hour-to-face interest rates for the 2017 fiscal year, the defense defense reimbursement rate for the VH-3D is 24,380 US dollars per hour of flying.
In the entries of the unit it is noted that the flight time in the air amounted to 30 minutes in each direction from his airfield at the aviation base of the Kuantiko marine in Virgina.
The White house claims that the real cost of using a helmet is much lower than this bet.
“RECOUNT the cost for taxpayers, based on an exemplivated rate of reimbursement, utenvity,” Walters said.
“These exemplary bets include personnel, maintenance and many other irreversible costs, which are included in the annual assignments.”
According to a study carried out in 2015 by RAND Corporation, compensation rates do not include the cost of personnel, but, in fact, take into account the cost of combustible, maintenance and the expenses specified in the contract.
At that time the former White House spokeswoman Sean Spicer spoke out in defense of using a helix for the event.
“It’s an idea to showcase things done in America this week,” Spicer said.
“And I’m aware that Sikorsky and Konnekkut are very proud of the fact that they are contributing to national security and that there are hundreds, if not thousands of people, whose workplace depends on it.
And I think, like the majority of the Americans, that we are all proud of this helix and other military equipment, the creation of which so many Americans worked tirelessly.
Therefore, of course, it is quite advisable to pay attention to it.”
It was incomprehensible whether trump interacted with the helix, inspecting the South lawn during the event, but he definitely slept in a driver's seat in a fire truck.
Inside the White House, trump appealed to Sikorsky, joking with the press about his own fleet of the company’s products.
“I know Sikorsky very well,” the president said.
Moscow will allocate grants for resuscitation departments of urban hospitals
Every year, "Rescue Life" grants will be allocated to resuscitations and intensive care units of the capital's medical clinics.
The funds will be used to encourage doctors and nurses.
The mayor of Moscow Sergey Sobyanin visited the Yudina City Clinical Hospital.
During the examination of the clinic, he presented a letter of gratitude to the doctor-traumatologist-ortopepad Viktor Protsko, under the leadership of which a complex operation was carried out to reconstruct the foot of a teenager.
Sergey Sobyanin also spoke about the decision to annually allocate grants to resuscitations and intensive care units of city clinics.
The funds will be used to encourage doctors and medical sisters.
According to the mayor of the capital's mayor, Yudin Clinical Hospital today is one of the largest in Moscow.
In recent years, the clinic has received a new modern equipment, allowing its doctors to carry out unique operations.
The clinic was opened in 1961 on the basis of the Kolomna Rural Hospital.
At the present time, the departments of the medical institution are designed to receive more than a thousand patients.
In addition to resuscitation and a hospital, there are daily departments here.
The staff of the hospital includes 2800 people.
The total area, occupying a medclinic, is 23.7 hectares.
In February of this year the medical institution became a participant of a pilot project for the organization of short-temporary stay hospitals (SKP).
They are designed to carry out relatively small operations.
In the course of surgical intervention, advanced medical equipment is used to significantly shorten the rehabilitation of patients.
After the operation in the hospital, they spend only a few hours.
Only in the first half of this year in the clinical hospital named after Yudina was provided with inpatient medical care to 36 thousand patients.
Medical employees of the clinic performed 15800 operations of a varying degree of complexity.
The NBU said about the absence of buyers of the Ukrainian “daughter” of Sberbank
In the national Bank of Ukraine (NBU) announced the absence of applications for the purchase of the Ukrainian “daughter” of Sberbank.
About it on Friday, August 4, reports TASS with reference to the representative of the press service of the NBU.
The NBU confirms that on August 3, 2017, a package of documents from a citizen of Belarus and Cyprus, Viktor Prokopen to coordinate the indirect (via Paritetbank) acquisition of 100 per cent shares of Sberbank was withdrawn.
“Documents from other potential investors did not arrive on the purchase of shares of Sberbank in the NBU”, – stated in the message.
On August 3, the Belarusian businessman Viktor Prokopenya withdrew the application for the purchase of a subsidiary of Sberbank.
On July 28, it became known that the National Bank of Ukraine rejected Russian businessmen Saida Gutseriev and Grigory Guselnikov in the acquisition of the Ukrainian “daughter” of Sberbank.
Regulator substantiated its decision by the fact that the businessmen did not provide the necessary documents for verification for their compliance with the requirements of the legislation of Ukraine.
Sberbank announced the sale of its Ukrainian “daughter” to Norvik Banka consortium and a private Belarusian company in March of this year.
The majority shareholder of the consortium was Said Gutseriev, the son of the Russian businessman Mikhail Gutseriev.
Sanctions against the “daughters” of the five Russian banks in Ukraine, including Sberbank, was introduced in mid-March.
Within a year, they are forbidden to withdraw capital from the country in favor of maternity organizations.
Trailer of the third season “Narco”: in the popular TV series studio “Netflix” after the death of Pablo Escobar, Kaly cartel plays a central role
