Democracies in Afghanistan depend on the role of women in politics, the UN said.
The elections can be representative only when they are attended by all members of society, including women, the head of the UN mission in Afghanistan said on Wednesday.
Nikolas Hays, according to Nikolas Jays, the reigning head of the U.N. assistance mission, hundreds of women are vARRISCONDs, three women are serving as vice-president, and more than 30 per cent of newly registered voters are women.
“The role of women cannot be overestimated,” he said in a statement on Wednesday.
Choices can be completely representative only when women participate fully and are included at all stages of the electoral process.
Provincial council elections and presidential elections will be held in Afghanistan on April 5.
“Talipolines threaten to thwart the electoral process that coincides with the transition of international forces from military operations to the role of advisers.
In this year's elections for the first time, power passes peacefully from one democratically elected government to another.
Hayse said that increasing the role of women will contribute to the success of democratic democracy in Afghanistan.
According to the Independent Electoral Commission of Afghanistan, out of a total of 3.6 million registered Voters, 1.2 million are women.
The Prosecutor General’s office approved the indictment in the case of Nikita Belykh
The Prosecutor General’s office of Russia approved the indictment in the criminal case against the former Governor of the Kirov region Nikita Bely, accused of receiving a large bribe.
About it on Thursday, August 3, was reported in the Department, reports RIA Novosti.
