In Venice tightened fines for tourists for inadvisible behavior
The Venetian authorities tightened fines for swimming in the canals from 50 euros to 500 euros.
For walking around the city in a swimsuit or with a naked torse will now be vaccinated for 200 euros.
For 100 euros will be demanded from those who will hold a picnic in a public place or ride a cycling in pedestrian areas, reports TASS with reference to the Association of Tour Operators of Russia.
In addition, it is mentioned that the authorities envisage a fine for inscriptions on monuments of 400 euros and for garbage of 25 euros.
Invoifting tourists about the need to observe the rules of conduct in Venice will be with the help of a special company "Peer, Respect the Ventilation" (#EnjoyRespecVenezia) in social networks, as well as through ads and posters on the website of the city council, on billboards and in the places of the largest congregation of tourists.
The campaign will be conducted in 10 lingacies.
According to the Tourism Advisor of Venice Paola Mar, information about fines will be transferred to the embassies of the relatives of violators, in order to prevent their compatriots from such mistakes.
“It’s a problem that Venice is perceived as a beach,” she said.
In April, the administration of the Italian city announced plans to limit the tourist flow.
In Venezia there is already a successful restriction on the number of tourists visiting the city center.
Instead of 100 000 people wishing to watch Festa del Redentore festival, only 60 000 guests were allowed to take place.
In addition, a moratorium has been imposed on the creation of new hotels and fast-fet food restaurants in the historical part of Venice.
Employees of the state border service in the first half of 2017 detained 272 illegal immigrants at the border with the EU countries; a total of 1,059 illegal migrants were detained.
This was reported in the state border service.
Of these, 314 people were detained for the illegal crossing of the border, and the rest - for violating the rules of residence of foreigners in Ukraine and other offenses.
The largest number - 717 illegal migrants were detained on the border with Moldova.
On the border with the EU, 272 illegal immigrants were detained, the majority of whom - on the border with Slovakia, Poland, Hungary and Romania.
According to the statistics, among the detained illegal immigrants are mainly citizens of Moldova, the Russian Federation, Georgia, Turkey, Azerbaijan, Bangladesh, Viet Nam, India and Armenia.
In addition, almost 2 thousand potential illegal migrants have not been occupied in Ukraine.
We will remind, in the EU found an unusual way to get rid of migrants.
Jazz in Skolkovo: an experiment and improvisation
Announced the program of the second Skolkovo Jazz Science festival, which will be held on August 26 at the Skolkovo innovation center.
Guests await the performances of leading jazz groups and soloists, scientific discussions, interactive venues and other musical and intellectual events.
As the organizers promise, the site will become an improvisation territory and a field to demonstrate new creative opportunities.
“Guests of the festival will be able to immerse ourselves in the world of experimental media technologies and learn how innovations in science are becoming a new tool of interaction with art,” Elena Zelentsova, vice-president of the Skolkovo Foundation, said.
Among the participants of Skolkovo Jazz Science 2017, there are a lot of stars, including Igor Bbutman's Moskovsky Jazz Orchestra, which will present a joint program with vocalist Yaroslava Simonova.
Jazz and science are treacherous concepts, and it is no coincidence that they are united, the people’s artist told Izvestia.
Jazzamp’s experiment and improvisation is valued just as high as scientists.
One of the main events of the festival will be the performance of Azekel, the Briton of Nigerian origin, known both for its own creativity and a joint work with the legendary Massive Attack and Gorillaz.
We are looking forward to the jazz fans of the first performance in Russia of a five-time Grammy nominee, pianist Christian Sands (USA) with his trio.
In a new capacity will try one of the best academeral chamber orchestras "Music Viva" under the guidance of Alexander Rudin and with the participation of pianist Yuri Favorin.
The merging of jazz, ethnic and electronic music, as well as academia traditions will be demonstrated by the Marimba Plus ensemble and its leader, composer and marimbe performer Lea Slepner.
One of the most unemerniest festival performances promises to be a set of prize laureate Sergey Kurekhin Anton Maskeliadze.
The artist-experitinator manages the music and video with the help of gestures - this is how leap motion technology works.
In total, eight musical groups will perform on two stages of the festival.
In addition, the program includes open discussions, interactive zones and art objects, united by the idea of merging music and science.
The guests will be able to take part in the experiments, visit a scientific buffet and observe the creation of cry-frost-frost-frost or brilliance of starch and water.
It will be possible to purchase records of relevant jazz performers and representatives of other musical directions in a special vinyl zone, and at the book fair - publications on various topics, including musical, popular scientific and biomedical literature.
SVF released Ozerov from the position of the head of the committee
The Federation Council on Wednesday supported the statement of the Chairman of the Committee on defense and security Viktor Ozerov and dismissed him from this position.
He remains a senator from the Khabarovsk Krai.
An application with a request to vacate him from his post Ozerov wrote last week.
He explained his decision with the need to rotate and his desire to “replace the rhythm of life”.
the senator also noted that the decision on leaving was not immediate.
Viktor Ozerov since 1996 has been presenting the Legislative Assembly of the Khabarovsk Territory in the Federation Council of the Russian Federation since 1996.
The senator has ruled the Defence and Security Committee since 2001.
Electricity is getting cheaper for both residents and educators of Buryatia
The efforts of the Soviet and post-Soviet authorities of the Republic of Buryatia (Vostoché Szbirsk), which have lasted more than a decade, to establish fair tariffs for consumers of electric energy are beginning to bear fruit.
From September 1, the cost of low-strength electricity for industrial receivers has been reduced by 25 per cent.
The federal antimonopoly service of the country in accordance with the Decree of the Government of the Russian Federation "On Amendments to the Rules of the Wholesaln Market of Electrical Energy and Possible and the Consolidated Probable Balancing of Electricity (capacitance) within the Unified Energy System of the Russian Federation" (17.07.2017 NO. 842) established indicative prices for electricity and capacity for industrial consumers of the Republic of Buryat.
As a result, the cost of electrical energy for Buryat educators is reduced by a quarter, which will greatly facilitate the life of small and medium-sized enterprises and individual entrepreneurs.
For many decades, the leaders of the republic have beaten the thresholds of the Moscow offices in vain attempts to equate the region in tariffs with a cascade of hydroelectric power plants on the Angara, flowing from Baikal, the main catchment area for which Buryatia.
It’s just this year that progress has begun.
In March, tariffs for electric energy for the population of the Republic were reduced from 4.24 rubles / kWh to 3.93 rubles / kWh, or by 7.3%.
With the incorporation of Buryatia according to the decision of the federal government in the list of territories of the price zones of the wholesale market, for which the functions of wholesale and retail markets are established the turn of industrial consumers are established.
According to analysts, this is only the beginning, since the population of the Irkutsk region pays 1.01 ruble for kilowatt/hour.
But no one dares to name the approximated date of the new tariff movement towards a decrease for Buryat.
