But wasn’t the football world been alerted about such an opportunity three years ago by PSG president?
“When “Manchester City” expressed an interest in hiring Blaise Matyuid in 2014, Nasser Al-Khelaifi gave a harsh warning to any club who would like to lure one of the best PSG players.
“I don’t worry, because they know that if they touch one of our players, then we’re going to stand up against it, we’re going to make proposals to their players,” Helaifi said.
“We are respectful of all clubs.
But if they try to recruit one of our players, the consequences await.”
“Barcelona seems to have crossed this trait when the Spanish club earlier this summer expressed an interest in PSG midfielder Marco Vertratti.
PSG made it clear that it will not let the Italian player of the national team on any conditions, and now, probably, “Barcelona” feels the consequences of its offer in the form of a loss of one of his most valuable players, Neymar.
